{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders","id":1004711,"title":"Storytelling Nephandi and Marauders","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-17T17:07:23-08:00","id":1004711,"title":"Storytelling Nephandi and Marauders","content":"I have the original Book of Madness, the revised Book of Madness and Mage 20. But, I'm still not sure how to run either group. Barabbi I more or less get, they subvert the organization they used to belong to. What do you do with Widderslainte?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T01:13:14-08:00","id":1004835,"title":"","content":"Widderslainte are treated as the &quot;mean kids in your neighbourhood that caused all kinds of stuff, sometimes quite disturbing too&quot; and those little maniacs grew up with much bigger ambitions and intentions, and to make it worse they were also Awakened.<br /> <br /> Some Widderslainte, however, instead struggle with that corrupted nature that stems from their Avatar. It is usually up to Storyteller what exact kind of Widderslainte is encountered - whether the one that wants to make your day a bad one, or the one seeking help and redemption - but as a rule of thumb, those are the people that /not neccessary/ have fallen into that situation by their own will. Barabbi choose to become what they are, Widderslainte are cursed with it.<br /> <br /> Though, the reason why there's so little Widderslainte that ever find redemption or remain on that path for long is because of how others are untolerant to them, and for a reason. Nephandi are notorious for all kinds of stuff that will make you have shivers going down your spine, and the fact that there's a guy claiming something like &quot;hey, I need help, I think I'm related to Nephandus&quot; would not really get them help but rather make others cautious, if not aggressive and violent towards the person.<br /> <br /> What else Widderslainte have to do? It is rare to find Widderslainte that tries to struggle with that inner seed of corruption, and even rarer to find someone who will understand them and try to help. They have no other choice but to join the ranks of Nephandi, else they'll most likely end up killed &quot;so that they can be cleansed in the next life&quot; by other Mages. Widderslainte are victims in this, often forced into fate they never chose on their own.<br /> <br /> As for Marauders, there's one big advise - do not treat Marauder's insanity as excuse for that Mage to be some sort of a comedian or clown. Marauder's insanity is a tragedy, often triggered by desperate events that occured in Mage's life. It's a burden they carry in lack of awareness about situation, and due to fact how often the &quot;silent Quiet&quot; (insanity that is hard to distingush) manifests, it is often too late to help Marauder once the insanity is apparent.<br /> <br /> There's a brief story about Mage who lost his wife and children, but his sorrow and despair was so intense to the point that he has fallen into Denial Quiet, simply refusing to believe they're gone. In his own world, his wife and children were still alive and well, but for others that insanity was not obvious. It was quite a heartbreaking thing to find out for other Mages once they realised what's going on - and could you even blame that man for falling into Quiet? His own consciousness refused to believe that his family is no more and he slipped into madness where he was actually happy, reunited with them once again.<br /> <br /> When storytelling Marauders and Nephandi, you have to keep in mind that it is in fact rare to encounter &quot;True Evil&quot;. Everyone is a hero and a victim in their own tale, and in the end a lot of Nephandi do not even think of themselves as something evil, just pragmatic enough to see that the world is going to hell anyway. Marauders are often the victim of their own gift after they Awakened, or something pretty bad happened to them during life which triggered the state of Quiet.<br /> <br /> Storytelling Marauders and Nephandi as some &quot;soulless monsters that just try to kill you every damn time&quot; gets boring too quick and repetitive, moreover there's far more depth to them that most assume.<br /> <br /> Hope this helped. If anything else, feel free to ask more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T07:22:02-08:00","id":1004924,"title":"","content":"For me, the act of turning Nephandi and getting your Avatar inverted in the Cauls doesn't make you Evil per se - it makes the feeling of fulfillment and satisfaction from higher things (helping a friend, seeing someone you love) instead come from lower impulses. So you would get the same feeling a normal person derives from comforting a loved one by instead harming or violating them. Nephandi aren't mind-controlled into evil, they are following a twisted superego.<br /> <br /> So for widderslainte, you can imagine someone who has these &quot;wrong&quot; impulses and feelings but doesn't know where they came from and didn't ask for them. They aren't forced to follow them, but denying it is like being asked to abandon someone you love. They'll never know true happiness because the only way their soul will give it to them is if they engage in destructive behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T07:44:25-08:00","id":1004932,"title":"","content":"I really like the concept of Widderslainte. When done right these characters can be the most sympathetic yet diabolical NPCs you'll come across.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Nephandi, the central theme is that of descent. Some are in it for the cathartic pleasure of destruction, some are in it because they hate the world and want to exact terminal revenge, and some are in it because they think reality is broken and only a hard reboot will do.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Barabbi, the big factor for them is that of choice, why did they choose to turn, and who they were influenced by?<br /> Did they go down the Joker route of having one bad day?<br /> Was it a gradual accumulation of events, with each good things gradually stripped away from them until they were left with nothing but hatred?<br /> Were they betrayed by someone who created their world view, their moral code, and now question whether morality even exists?<br /> Were they seduced by the power offered by the Nephandi, and have a desire for subversive control?<br /> Have they been tricked into helping the Nephandi, and now no one will trust them, leaving only the Nephandi as their source of companionship?<br /> Or do they simply think the Traditions are as bad as the Technocrats, that humanity is fundamentally evil and no one truly deserves ascension?<br /> <br /> Widderlsainte, on the other hand, don't get a choice. This is them from the start, trapped with a tainted avatar who seeks only destruction.<br /> <br /> The first question for them is how well they agree with their avatar?<br /> Are they aware of the evil intent of their sou, or are they blissfully ignorant of the destruction their seemingly innocuous actions cause?<br /> Once made aware, do they try to fight it, or do they recognise it as a losing battle early on and give in?<br /> Do they seek help or do others try to help them before they are indoctrinated into the Nephandi properly?<br /> Do they like themselves? Do they act only as a puppet for their powerful avatars or are they the ones in control and merely use their avatars to fuel their instinctual desire for destruction?<br /> Are they afraid of what they are capable off?<br /> Is their avatar the only source of comfort they have from a cruel and uncaring world, one filled with those who think their death makes it a better place?<br /> <br /> Another thing worth consideration is who their avatar belonged to before them. Are they a long line of widderslainte or was this avatar corrupted merely a generation ago?<br /> How does this affect the relationship between Widderslainte and Avatar?<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding Marauders, I like to split them up into a few categories.<br /> <br /> The first is Humans with Neurological/Mental illnesses who happen to be magic.<br /> If you've read &quot;The Man Who Mistook his Wife for a Hat&quot;, you'll get a great deal of real life neurological disease stricken patients, any number of whom could be good inspiration for a marauder. The titular Man was a music teacher who steadily lost the ability to associate visual data with archetypal meaning. He'd see a glove, for example, and would recognise the colour, the shape, the fact that it had five protruding lumps, but wouldn't realise it was a glove until he accidentally put in on, at first he thought it might have been a coin purse designed to keep certain coins separate. Taken externally, a Marauder like this would live in a world of constant flux, doors would suddenly disappear, replaced with a light bulb sticking on the side of a shelf. Paintings become windows and landscapes could resemble paintings made by Magritte. So to mages that approach this man would turn into objects, or objects into animals. To the Marauder all of this is normal.<br /> The underlying theme of these Marauders is one of disconnection and isolation. Through no fault of their own, the world has become vastly different from others, preventing them from being able to interact with others for any meaningful length of time. They may be considered dangerous, or at the very least too unstable to rely on, and thus are socially cut off from the rest of mage society, doomed to be confined to their own bubbles of reality. Though perhaps not. There could be many Marauders who's mental illness is subtle enough that it is hard to distinguish from normal magical effects, and thus must fight against the world trying to maintain the facade of health as they constantly question whether what they are experiencing is real or their, and if even such a difference holds any merit. The fear of ostracism is ever present, as is the desire to either &quot;cure&quot; themselves, or find some environment where they can just be themselves free from persecution. <br /> <br /> The second are Stuck in Fiction.<br /> These guys are either fans of a specific series of books or mythos. They are so struck by these worlds that they literally see they are convinced that they are living in these worlds and may even be characters within this story. Not unlike Don Quixote, these mages will assume the role of hero in their story and will transform events around them in order to match key narrative points. They may see themselves as Peter Pan, and thus your group of mages may transform into a horde of pirates, they may see themselves as Batman, and the streets around them become Gotham, with every Mage transformed into some character, perhaps the Verbena witch become Poison Ivy, or your Virtual Adept friend into one of the many iterations of The Riddler. Explosions become frequent, and the tone can shift drastically from silver age camp to modern day horror depending on the mood of the Marauder in question.<br /> They aren't limited to hero's however, they could be other characters, perhaps they think themselves as Sir Lancelot, desperately searching for King Arthur. You could also make them villains from these stories, but this is much harder to do while keeping them sympathetic.<br /> These kinds of Marauders play on the idea of self actualisation, they want so badly to be the hero of these stories, that they lose themselves to it and forget their previous lives. To do that with an outright villain archetype will be much more difficult to sympathise with.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, they may see themselves as an average Joe trapped in the world they've conjured around themselves, trying to escape but unable to comprehend that it is them that creates their trap. The chronicle I'm running right now deals with such an unfortunate, trapped in the world described by H.P. Lovecraft.<br /> <br /> The Third are Stuck in Time.<br /> Like the Stuck in Fiction group, except rather than a specific narrative, these guys are convinced that they are within a specific time period, be it Victorian England, Ancient Rome, The Sengoku Jidai, or even the 80s. While it's not impossible to find such Marauders who believe themselves to be historic characters, it's more likely that they'd consider their surroundings to be analogous to the time period they find themselves in. It may not necessarily be a historically accurate period, but rather one fuelled by the beliefs and prejudices of the day. Perhaps in this Marauders Ancient Greece, gods are literally walking amongst men as they were thought to do at the time. Perhaps they see themselves in the South Africa at the height of the apartheid, and can't help but seeing anyone non-white as literally animal like, forcing such a transformation upon them, while the white people look in some way more human (sensitive topic, I know. Be aware of what's appropriate in your group).<br /> The theme for these Marauders is one of displacement. They live in a reality which once was, but has since been discarded. The world has moved on but the mage is trapped, either left behind or simply unable to accept the world they are presented with in favour of their current beliefs. Their madness can take the form of Denial, where anything that does not fit into their time frame simply doesn't exist or is a much older model. Theirs is an attitude of revisionism. They will most likely justify their own beliefs by virtue of their own experience, and will be entirely incapable of accepting what they don't already believe to be true. Even events they have performed themselves may have simple &quot;not happened&quot; if it goes against what they're used to. Not unlike those with the Sleepwalker flaw.<br /> <br /> The Fourth are Trauma Survivors.<br /> These poor Mages are those who have endured a great deal of stress from a series of traumatic events. Perhaps they were kidnapped and tortured, perhaps they were abused as children, perhaps sadistic forces kept throwing everything they could until they eventually snapped. These are mages that may have become Barabbi had they not snapped first, or instead chose specifically not to join the nephandi and thus were left no alternative than to withdraw into their own minds for safety.<br /> One version of these Marauders are those who have retreated entirely into a self made safe space, maybe a warm bed in their room, a cool meadow by a river, or their mother's loving embrace, anything that does not fit in with the feelings of safety are banned from entry or transformed in some way. The avatar is so consumed with healing the Mage that nothing else matters. However, their safe little world may start to fray at the edges, slowly unravelling after enough external influence forces the Mage to confront the reality they've been pushing away.<br /> They may alternatively see themselves as children lost in an uncaring world, and become a child in turn. They may see themselves as the one to blame for their victimhood, and thus manifest their hatred and fear as external forces, perhaps as demons, perhaps as snakes, perhaps simply as angry men with chains. These marauders are often unable to stay stable for very long and may be easily triggered into reliving the moments of their attack of seeing the people involved. Perhaps they are done being scared and hopeless and will attempt to fight their inner demons.<br /> The themes of these Marauders is one of being broken and dealing with the shattered pieces, and whether or not it's possible to mend completely if at all, and how much damage one may inadvertently cause to their surroundings in the process. A question of self vs those around them, and the struggle against the memories that pull at them.<br /> <br /> The Fifth are Sufferers of Loss.<br /> This is example given by Bogdan above, a Marauder who fell to madness as a way of coping with a heavy loss. It could be, as described above, that they refuse to believe their family had been lost and so may project the roles of their family members on to other people, or simply still &quot;live&quot; with their lost family at home. In the reverse, their family may have left them for one reason or another, and to deal with this feeling of abandonment, they invented the narrative of their death by the hands of another, perhaps creating a Revenge archetype character not unlike that seen in Memento. Another angle on this is a Mage who is convinced that they themselves are dead and are in fact a ghost. They may exhibit many facets of being a Wraith, but are not actually in the Dark umbra, and spirit magic has no effect. They may believe that they have died and their family and friends moved on without them when in reality their morbid musings drove them away. They may believe that they had been killed by someone innocent and now seek to exact misplaced revenge. They may in fact think they are dead but trapped in their own body. Perhaps their body will start to decay as they become more engrossed in this theory, perhaps they may even try to &quot;escape&quot; their body, but find every attempt of there's fails because they are in some way indestructible, yet at no point will their body feel likes &quot;theirs&quot; anymore, it's is simply a lump of dead flesh they can't seem to shake off.<br /> The major theme here is that of denial and an inability to accept things as they are. They have lost something, something they can't bare to be without, and so their mind and avatar invents something to make sense of this loss. Unlike the Trauma Survivors who would do anything to gain back their normalcy, these Marauders will go through any measure to keep their illusions alive. Facing the world they have rejected is not an option anymore.<br /> <br /> The Sixth are Trapped by Hubris<br /> These are very high level Mages, perhaps even Archmages who have attained a great level of understanding in how the universe operates. Maybe they've been the mastermind behind incredibly ambitious projects of Council level interest, maybe they've even spent time in a couple of Horizon realms or Deep Umbra Worlds, or maybe they are reclusive individuals obsessed with their particular area of study. The point is that they've reached a level of understanding beyond what most mages achieve, and have become so absorbed with their paradigm that literally no other form of magic or science makes sense to them. They know how the world works, they are certain about it down to the smallest drop, and that's how things simply are. These Marauders are like mini Horizon Realms in and of themselves, creating new paradox rules and Reality Zones just by their very presence. They have a &quot;logical&quot; explanation or reason for anything that flies in the face of their reality, and for anything that doesn't, it simply morphs into something that does, or just doesn't exist.<br /> These are the Marauders that all Mages are susceptible to becoming, and some may argue that the vast majority of Masters are already half way there. Their theme is that of the dangers of extremist ideology, of creating echo chambers around one's self, and of considering one's own reasoning to be infallible. It is the fate of all those who do not wish to examine their own ideas with scrutiny, and consider that perhaps they have been wrong all this time.<br /> <br /> That's about all I can think up right now. All of these Marauders can be down with any variety of Quiet, and nothing says you can't have a Marauder that fits into multiple categories. The big thing to remember when making a Marauder is:<br /> A) They are human at their core.<br /> B) They believe in their Quiet very strongly.<br /> C) They are most likely unaware of what they are, and even if they are, they can't know the full extent of their madness. None of us can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T07:50:56-08:00","id":1004933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1004932#post1004932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to Nephandi, the central theme is that of descent. Some are in it for the cathartic pleasure of destruction, some are in it because they hate the world and want to exact terminal revenge, and some are in it because they think reality is broken and only a hard reboot will do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I am annoyed that while there are three very distinct and different factions of Nephandi, with different goals and origins, that this is used as their common central theme.<br /> <br /> Both the Infernal Nephandi as well as those who are worshipping the Cthulhuesque totally-not-elder-gods are not thematically after destruction for destruction's sake, nor a reboot of everything. Their central theme is either a tragic lust of power, circumstances that led them into a bad deal, or plain insanity-induced worship. The destroy-everything kind of Nephandi are probably a rarity among those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T08:32:12-08:00","id":1004963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1004933#post1004933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I am annoyed that while there are three very distinct and different factions of Nephandi, with different goals and origins, that this is used as their common central theme.<br /> <br /> Both the Infernal Nephandi as well as those who are worshipping the Cthulhuesque totally-not-elder-gods are not thematically after destruction for destruction's sake, nor a reboot of everything. Their central theme is either a tragic lust of power, circumstances that led them into a bad deal, or plain insanity-induced worship. The destroy-everything kind of Nephandi are probably a rarity among those.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this was addressed in the Book of Madness. Not all Infernalists are Nephandi. Those who have sold their soul to the devil for some Faustian agreement are not Nephandic, they are simply really foolish Mages/whatever who lust for power and sacrifice the long term in favour of short term gain. Infernalist Nephandi, on the other hand, are the guys who are helping such agreements take place. They don't assist their demon god because of pure personal gain, but because they believe their demon god has the right idea. If the world's going to hell anyway, might as well get a good seat.<br /> <br /> In order to have your avatar inverted, you have to actively believe the nephandic ideal of destruction, it's not enough to rely on doing it for personal gain. Inverting your Avatar is a one way street to irredeemable levels, you cut off ascension from yourself, and devote your existence to cutting it away from everyone else.<br /> If you want to have Power Lusting Infernalists in your game, go ahead, but they aren't Nephandi.<br /> <br /> As for the K'llashaa, they may not be worshippers of Azathoth style &quot;Destroy Everything&quot; gods, but they are certainly for the idea of getting rid of this sorry excuse for a planet. Either that or they know a &quot;hidden&quot; truth that they bring upon themselves to make real to the rest of humanity, whether they want it or not.<br /> Point is that they may not be for the destruction of all things, but they are certainly for bringing down humanities ideas of how they think the universe works, because &quot;they know better&quot;, they know the words of the elder gods, the things that man was not meant to know, ideas only seen in dreams from distant stars, and once the stars are right, their glory and power will be brought back unto this world where they can reshape reality in their own image.<br /> <br /> I'ya Yog-Sothoth Kadishtu Nilgh'ri!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T09:28:41-08:00","id":1004980,"title":"","content":"The one time I really used Widderslainte, I definitely went in for the &quot;tragic&quot; angle. A central conceit of the whole game was that the PCs were a group of companion souls that had been &quot;reincarnated&quot; (for whatever value of &quot;soul&quot; and &quot;Avatar&quot; you buy into) over a vast swath of time, and had, in fact, been critically important personages at pivotal points in Mage history. (E.g. one character had been both Baldric La Salle and Tytalus in previous lives.... 'Cause, why not? It was a &quot;Go Big or Go Home&quot; kinda chronicle). The game started off with the characters starting to cross lives pre-Awakening. The story that was set in the midst of all their Awakenings involved a mass homicide of a family and the kidnapping of the one survivor, an adolescent girl. They rescued her. Took care of her since she was all alone in the world. Became her ersatz parents. And.... she was one the &quot;travelling souls&quot;. The one who had Fallen. So they got to know her when she was definitely struggling and tortured, but they were also there when she Awakened and realizes who and what she was. It was wrenching and awful (and lots of wonderful role-playing). One PC willingly gave his life to try to keep it from happening. It didn't stop it. She killed him She KNEW she loved these peoples and had loved them across many lives, but it didn't change who or what she was. She wept as she set off (flew off, actually) to start wrecking ruin on the world...<br /> <br /> Overall, it went pretty well, as far as I could tell.<br /> <br /> Another character in another game had some suppressed memories of a childhood where his cousin was a Bad Seed who, at age 10, did all those things attributed to budding serial killers and was able to intimidate the younger version of the character into silence. The kind was, obviously, a Widderslainte. When the two met in the course of the game, the once Bad Seed kid, now accomplished Nephandus, there was definitely some very interesting interaction. First, with the &quot;Surely, you must remember..&quot; Followed by the remembering. Followed by near-vendetta levels of attempted thwarting of Nephandi plans. It definitely made the whole things personal.<br /> <br /> I think that's the only time I really used Widderslainte. The other Nephandi have been Barrabi. Either the &quot;hidden disease from within&quot; type or out there accomplishing their evil ends after having left their old groups behind. Plus a Nephandus or two that was converted so soon after Awakening that they were never really anything other than a Nephandus. <br /> <br /> I really haven't used Marauders as much. I have had some ideas for future chronicles that definitely could correct that. The one I recall offhand was a lonely neglected boy who Awakened and started seeing the whole world as a computer game, quests and all. He didn't come across as different from a really focused Orphan at the start. The cabal even tried to hook him up with their VA allies to get him &quot;trained up&quot;. Eventually his Quiet deepened and became a significant problem as he started reformatting the world around him to fit with his &quot;game&quot;. (People do pretty destructive and antisocial things as the heroes of those kind of games...) They eventually put him into a coma and left him there while they desultorily tried to find a cure. They hadn't done so by the end of the chronicle. Later on, there was a spin-off Vampire mini-chronicle where the same players with new vampire characters in the same setting slightly later met the character again. A local Malkavian Elder who was cozy with some wraiths recognized the issues the dreaming Marauder was beginning to have on reality in his area. Said elder tried his own version of a &quot;cure&quot; by embracing him...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T10:36:08-08:00","id":1005020,"title":"","content":"There's a subtle aspect to Marauders I don't see used very often. Every other Mage fights against the wall that is reality. Even the most hubristic of Mages will run into the consequences of their actions, the reactions of other people, or the misbehavior of other people. They may try to turn a blind eye, but there are thousands of little cues that draw mages back towards coherency and consistency.<br /> <br /> Most Marauders have none of that. They are permanently insulated from dealing with the fallout they (and their Avatars) don't want to feel. Nothing stops them from embracing nonsensical and contradictory ideas. Nothing stops them from spiraling further and further from any semblance of an understandable world view. Many people try to make their madness relateable, either by drawing on known mental conditions or simple tragedies, but even if their Quiets start that way, there's no reason they will stay like that. They are adrift.<br /> <br /> Like the sailors of old, they lost sight of land and there are no stars to guide them back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T14:30:24-08:00","id":1007434,"title":"","content":"Anyone from Lost Dreams stay out!<br /> <br /> Our resident NWO Operative has no idea they're a Widderslainte. They were found before Awakening by a <i>b</i><i>arabbus, </i>then paid to kill a Nephandic pawn who had outlived his usefulness. Three-fourths of their Genius is safe, because it's metaphysically insane and residing in the person of a Union-Sanctioned (near) Marauder. <br /> <br /> The <i>barabbus</i> is restraining the Widderslainte's corruption with Mind 5; leaving them an otherwise helpful and normal -- if fugue-ridden -- person. Either they'll die spectacularly, or someone can try for redemption. Somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T18:36:23-08:00","id":1018987,"title":"","content":"To be honest, having your avatar inverted sounds a lot like taking the red pill in Matrix:<br /> It's irreversible, you end demonized, hunted and rejected even by the people who portray themselves as the good guys, it is told to remove your free will and autonomy, it turns you into an evil bogeyman right after everyone took so many pains to explain how the universe was made of competing paradigms without absolute evil or good.<br /> <br /> Strange isn't it? How can everyone be so sure that inverting an avatar can alter someone so profoundly, to the point of this following through reincarnations, if they themselves never inverted their avatars? Seems an excuse to hunt opposition, Minority Report tier, &quot;you are evil from another life, here, let me you tell all about the things you will do if I don't kill you&quot;. &quot;You don't have free will, your opinions and objectives are not as legitimate as mine&quot;. How people have such a established view about something and its effect if they never experienced it themselves? How others accept such simple explanations while ignoring the reality of power of factional war?<br /> <br /> Maybe other mages are just sleepers themselves in comparison to mages who had their avatars inverted, and their limited souls interpret the enlightenment of Widderslaintes as something absurd, as destruction, as evil, as suffering, as nihilistic. Maybe this is why no one can clearly elaborate about the Nephandi and their objectives; it's all bullshit, blind people touching an elephant. Or maybe it's just propaganda, naivety, brainwashing and a casus belli against an opposing faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T19:13:16-08:00","id":1018997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1018987#post1018987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, having your avatar inverted sounds a lot like taking the red pill in Matrix:<br /> It's irreversible, you end demonized, hunted and rejected even by the people who portray themselves as the good guys, it is told to remove your free will and autonomy, it turns you into an evil bogeyman right after everyone took so many pains to explain how the universe was made of competing paradigms without absolute evil or good.<br /> <br /> Strange isn't it? How can everyone be so sure that inverting an avatar can alter someone so profoundly, to the point of this following through reincarnations, if they themselves never inverted their avatars? Seems an excuse to hunt opposition, Minority Report tier, &quot;you are evil from another life, here, let me you tell all about the things you will do if I don't kill you&quot;. &quot;You don't have free will, your opinions and objectives are not as legitimate as mine&quot;. How people have such a established view about something and its effect if they never experienced it themselves? How others accept such simple explanations while ignoring the reality of power of factional war?<br /> <br /> Maybe other mages are just sleepers themselves in comparison to mages who had their avatars inverted, and their limited souls interpret the enlightenment of Widderslaintes as something absurd, as destruction, as evil, as suffering, as nihilistic. Maybe this is why no one can clearly elaborate about the Nephandi and their objectives; it's all bullshit, blind people touching an elephant. Or maybe it's just propaganda, naivety, brainwashing and a casus belli against an opposing faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting angle, certainly, though it does severely change the dynamics of the Mage factions if the Nephandi are actually misunderstood enlightened individuals who have actually learned the truth.<br /> <br /> It means that everyone else, the Technocracy, the Traditions, even the Crafts and the Sleepers are fundamentally wrong about everything, and only the nephandi are right, the universe needs to be destroyed and to allow it to persist is in itself the path to destruction. The problem with Nephandi actually being &quot;the good guys&quot; is why are they known for encouraging corruption, causing suffering, spreading disease, and in general doing a lot of painful and unethical things to their subjects. They employ isolation, blackmail. murder, rape, and all kinds of manipulation to attack, corrupt, and recruit whoever they can find. Why would they do this if they were &quot;the good guys&quot;?<br /> <br /> You might say that they don't actually do this, that this is all propaganda designed to silence them and keep the real truth silent. But then you're basically creating your own content. Nothing in the game itself supports this viewpoint. Nephandi are emphatically evil in the eyes of the source material, and even the very best interpretation of them has them as thinking reality is broken and requires a hard reboot, so everything that exists right now, the people and their happiness, the universe and its supposed order, is all irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T05:24:19-08:00","id":1019175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1018987#post1018987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, having your avatar inverted sounds a lot like taking the red pill in Matrix:<br /> It's irreversible, you end demonized, hunted and rejected even by the people who portray themselves as the good guys, it is told to remove your free will and autonomy, it turns you into an evil bogeyman right after everyone took so many pains to explain how the universe was made of competing paradigms without absolute evil or good.<br /> <br /> Strange isn't it? How can everyone be so sure that inverting an avatar can alter someone so profoundly, to the point of this following through reincarnations, if they themselves never inverted their avatars? Seems an excuse to hunt opposition, Minority Report tier, &quot;you are evil from another life, here, let me you tell all about the things you will do if I don't kill you&quot;. &quot;You don't have free will, your opinions and objectives are not as legitimate as mine&quot;. How people have such a established view about something and its effect if they never experienced it themselves? How others accept such simple explanations while ignoring the reality of power of factional war?<br /> <br /> Maybe other mages are just sleepers themselves in comparison to mages who had their avatars inverted, and their limited souls interpret the enlightenment of Widderslaintes as something absurd, as destruction, as evil, as suffering, as nihilistic. Maybe this is why no one can clearly elaborate about the Nephandi and their objectives; it's all bullshit, blind people touching an elephant. Or maybe it's just propaganda, naivety, brainwashing and a casus belli against an opposing faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Matrix shows that even movies about terrorist cells with utterly callous attitudes towards innocent bystanders can work if you have good special effects and a kickass soundtrack. Pray the Nephandi never get either of those.<br /> <br /> All joking aside, that's certainly an argument a Nephandi would make, and I dare say more than one mage has gone to the cauls on that rationale. Nephandi can be very convincing and the idea shouldn't be one every Mage can ignore. In those dark moments of the soul, when nothing seems to fit together, there should always be that persistent question: what if they are right? It's a great element in an antagonist.<br /> <br /> You could even run the game that way if you wanted to, although I'm not sure what difference it would make. They are inscrutable either way, whether that's because of enlightenment or mutilation, so their place in the story doesn't change. Unless you put something in to show they are right (and I wouldn't recommend that) or that they are the victims of a massive propaganda campaign (which would be hard to explain well) it doesn't change much about them.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind that Nephandi aren't the only beings that Mages can't understand. Marauders and Oracles also occupy that space. And Oracles at least, have a much better claim on enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T05:54:51-08:00","id":1019181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1018997#post1018997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why are they known for encouraging corruption, causing suffering, spreading disease, and in general doing a lot of painful and unethical things to their subjects. They employ isolation, blackmail. murder, rape, and all kinds of manipulation to attack, corrupt, and recruit whoever they can find. Why would they do this if they were &quot;the good guys&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Such actions are the reality of power of the ascension war: everyone does that to enemies. Am I to naively believe in good guys?<br /> <br /> &quot;I want to destroy the world, muaha!&quot; is a childish anime villain trope, specially when it comes without reasons or justification besides sadism and nihilism. Sounds like propaganda to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing in the game itself supports this viewpoint. </div> </div> </div>I know, it's futile over-analysis and head canon. It's even shitposting and I'm sorry for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","user":"visigoth","date":". 12-19-2016, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T06:25:05-08:00","id":1019186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019175#post1019175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Matrix shows that even movies about terrorist cells with utterly callous attitudes towards innocent bystanders can work if you have good special effects and a kickass soundtrack.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly the reason for my comparison rather than a buddhist ending the cycle of suffering or a gnostic fighting against the false god.<br /> In Matrix you have people who undergo a massive irreversible experience and they come back to their previous reality with contempt and destructive impulses towards it. Innocent bystanders are at best useful idiots and at worst potential matrix agents. Of course that such people would seem immoral, unethical and evil to someone living in the Matrix; it is telling that only oracle or archmaster tier <s>brainwashing</s> magick can &quot;fix&quot; a reversed avatar.<br /> Of course traditions and technocracy would equally oppose nephandi, they are the prison wards, they are the collaborating prisoners of the grand gulag of life and they don't want to give away the power they acquired in this prison, they are confortable thinking of themselves as reality bending gods, even if they can't see behind the iron bars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","user":"visigoth","date":". 12-19-2016, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T08:45:07-08:00","id":1019263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019186#post1019186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is exactly the reason for my comparison rather than a buddhist ending the cycle of suffering or a gnostic fighting against the false god.<br /> In Matrix you have people who undergo a massive irreversible experience and they come back to their previous reality with contempt and destructive impulses towards it. Innocent bystanders are at best useful idiots and at worst potential matrix agents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should point out here that the same imagery also makes a good analogy for joining the Traditions as a whole, for joining more than half of the individual Traditions, and in some cases, for joining the Technocracy. Morpheus set his crew up as a mystery cult, so it's not surprising that it parallels many insular organizations that claim to lead people to wisdom and enlightenment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course that such people would seem immoral, unethical and evil to someone living in the Matrix; it is telling that only oracle or archmaster tier <s>brainwashing</s> magick can &quot;fix&quot; a reversed avatar. </div> </div> </div>Have they ever given sphere levels for the Cauls? I honestly can't remember, but I always picture them as being Archmaster level magic in their own right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course traditions and technocracy would equally oppose nephandi, they are the prison wards, they are the collaborating prisoners of the grand gulag of life and they don't want to give away the power they acquired in this prison, they are confortable thinking of themselves as reality bending gods, even if they can't see behind the iron bars. </div> </div> </div>If we are going to approach MtAsc gnostically (which I don't usually) I would consider the Nephandi to be one of the traps on the way to escape. The cheap revelation that requires magical tricks (the cauls) rather than actual seeking. Perhaps from their own point of view they are doing the world a favor by tearing down the prison, but if they are so busy attacking the bars that they miss the open door (Ascension) they have no claim on enlightenment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T10:36:27-08:00","id":1019326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019263#post1019263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point out here that the same imagery also makes a good analogy for joining the Traditions as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's a common trope and a cheap comparison, but the nephandic initiation is the only one without sleeper counterpart in culture or religions and that leaves permanent residual change. A normal avatar is shadow play or broken radio in comparison to inverted avatars, and an observer might argue that the inverted avatar is its fixed state, travelling between incarnations and giving the appereance of no free will.<br /> Nephandi are the opposite of Seers of the Throne of Awakening: they worship or serve isolated beings without influence in the world, they wield small power, and they seek to overthrow the status quo rather than maintain or profit from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> they are so busy attacking the bars that they miss the open door </div> </div> </div>This is why I can't buy the &quot;destroy the world&quot; objective. If they want to destroy it, what rape, corruption, suffering accomplish besides creating a small resonance and large attention? Breaking some irons bars doesn't destroy the prison. By this view, even being associated with infernalists is detrimental to the overall nephandic end game because this sticks evil to their image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T11:24:36-08:00","id":1019344,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019326#post1019326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's a common trope and a cheap comparison, but the nephandic initiation is the only one without sleeper counterpart in culture or religions and that leaves permanent residual change.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sad thing is that Nephandi do have a sleeper counterpart. Terrorism. I'm not talking just about Jihad and other forms of political terrorism, but about all forms of terrorism from school shootings, to hate crimes, and even slavery and people trafficking. Any group that reduces human life to little more than a means to an end is the kind of spirit that the nephandi thrive on. While the Marauders can arguably be the psychopaths of the awakened world, the Nephandi are the sociopaths, the sadists, and the extremists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019326#post1019326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why I can't buy the &quot;destroy the world&quot; objective. If they want to destroy it, what rape, corruption, suffering accomplish besides creating a small resonance and large attention? Breaking some irons bars doesn't destroy the prison. By this view, even being associated with infernalists is detrimental to the overall nephandic end game because this sticks evil to their image.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some nephandi want to destroy the world because they believe ascension to be a lie as you say, though others may do so simply because they believe humanity to be unworthy of ascension at all. They see the suffering that humanity causes and have come to the conclusion that humans are inherently evil, and in the same way the only truly noble act a vampire can commit is walking out into the midday sun, the only true act of selflessness is suicide. Humanity is a disease that needs to be taken care of at the source.<br /> <br /> Those with such a mindset may see corruption, rape, and other methods of abuse and control as tools for a greater plan. If they can bring others over to their way of thinking, either though pushing them to the very edge of madness until all they can accept is their own hatred for the world. Force them to become alienated and become ostracised by their peers until the nephandi are all they can turn to. Or simply allow them to realise what strength there is in admitting to yourself that humanity is fundamentally evil at heart. If you accept that you have evil within your heart, it becomes all the easier to see the evil in others. Destroy all notion of good, wake up to the inherent selfishness of all things everyone does, and get to work bringing about the end. Bring the people what they deserve.<br /> <br /> The clever nephandi will be able to reap destruction with a minimal of effort. All they need do is implant ideas in people's minds and watch as humanity tears itself apart, falling under the weight of their own inherent greed. But a less subtle approach can be even more effective if done correctly. Rape a woman, let her attacker go free. Have the police blame her for it, have her family so ashamed they disown her, have her realise how little society cares for her once she is tainted, show her how quick the world is to deny the legitimacy of her suffering and label her a fraud, a liar, and a whore. Let her internalise this deep injustice into a frothing pool of rage, and point it back at the very people who wronged her. Either she'll become a soldier for corruption, or she'll die in hatred and injustice, either way helps their cause. For no man is an island, and what one thinks is one's own private suffering will have knock on effect on every other person they come into contact with. Pass on the misery, never share it, just spread it. Let mankind's own selfish nature become its own undoing.<br /> <br /> While a lot of this is quite fitting for the Malfeans and their general desire to encourage the end through the strength of the Wyrm. The Infernalists too get something out of this. Their chosen dark ones gains power through a particular kind of suffering, be it the torture of an innocent child, the destruction of ones entire legacy, or simply the arbitration of the Faustian deal. The Infernalits are all out to make their Dark One as powerful and as influential as they can. After all, if the world is going to hell anyway, they better get themselves a damned good seat.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, some Nephandi are simply sexual deviants and get off on causing horrific acts. It satisfies them on many levels, not least because their avatar may reward them for such behaviour, but also because they just happen to be incredibly sick people even without an inverted avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T11:27:30-08:00","id":1019346,"title":"","content":"Is it worthwhile for a Demon Lord to invest in Nephandi? Given the rarity of Mages (1:100,000 in Revised), Nephandi are probably no more than 5% of them (1:2,000,000), I think that Demon Lords would get more bang for their buck converting angst ridden teenagers into Infernal Sorcerers. <br /> <br /> The Demon Lords would enter the dreams of the abused teenage girls, offer them some lesser powers in exchange for minor violations (consensual sex with dozens of adult men, dealing drugs at high school, desecration of churches, etc) and, when they high on easy power, offer them a soul pact for even greater power. Demon Lords could use a group of Infernal Sorcerer abused teenagr girls to destroy the entire social fabric of a small town by seducing adult men and revealing every dirty little secret of the town. When the town starts to burn, the Demon Lords would have them change their names and relocate to another small town, where they would recruit more abused teenage girls so they could destroy that town even faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T11:45:15-08:00","id":1019354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019346#post1019346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it worthwhile for a Demon Lord to invest in Nephandi? Given the rarity of Mages (1:100,000 in Revised), Nephandi are probably no more than 5% of them (1:2,000,000), I think that Demon Lords would get more bang for their buck converting angst ridden teenagers into Infernal Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> The Demon Lords would enter the dreams of the abused teenage girls, offer them some lesser powers in exchange for minor violations (consensual sex with dozens of adult men, dealing drugs at high school, desecration of churches, etc) and, when they high on easy power, offer them a soul pact for even greater power. Demon Lords could use a group of Infernal Sorcerer abused teenagr girls to destroy the entire social fabric of a small town by seducing adult men and revealing every dirty little secret of the town. When the town starts to burn, the Demon Lords would have them change their names and relocate to another small town, where they would recruit more abused teenage girls so they could destroy that town even faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>That ratio was only because so many of them were in the Umbra when the Avatar Storm hit. Unless you're running a game set in the early millennium, the chances are the number of awakened people on earth has expanded quite a bit.<br /> <br /> Let's not forget, however, that even with numbers that low, 1 mage can out perform an entire group of sorcerers with very little trouble. Sorcerers run out of Willpower pretty frequently, and can sometimes need a few days to recover from larger rituals, Mages have no such limit. Sure they may have to be careful of paradox, but if their effects are subtle enough it barely matters. If a Tradition or Technocratic mage becomes aware of a Nephandic group of sorcerors, it won't be too difficult to find them, round them up, and end them without too much trouble as their powers or tech will be far and above anything the sorcerer would be capable of.<br /> <br /> Awakened mages, on therefor a much grander prize. Their potency is much greater, their abilities require much less time and are a heck of a lot more effective. But their does lie one other great incentives to recruit awakened mages. Being able to fight against the Tradition and Technocratic forces which seek to end their plans. This doesn't just work to match like with like fire power, it also allows a foothold for further corruption. What better way to tear down against the enemy, than having the enemy convert to ally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T12:05:42-08:00","id":1019361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019326#post1019326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I can't buy the &quot;destroy the world&quot; objective. If they want to destroy it, what rape, corruption, suffering accomplish besides creating a small resonance and large attention? Breaking some irons bars doesn't destroy the prison. By this view, even being associated with infernalists is detrimental to the overall nephandic end game because this sticks evil to their image.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are either carrying out their evil acts or they aren't. If they aren't, if as you suggested their destructive nihilism is just a rationalization by mages who can't understand them, then they can't help their associations. If they are, and their actions are real and befit whatever enlightenment they think they have, then their associations are intentional (if inscrutable). Changing their end goal doesn't help much, because even their actions don't have to match up with any plan we can fathom.<br /> <br /> There could be, of course. Pain and suffering could be their lures to draw other destructive entities in. They could also be trying to alter the nature of the consensus by driving everyone to desire annihilation. But there doesn't have to be a rational rationale.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T12:49:06-08:00","id":1019371,"title":"","content":"It sounds like you'd enjoy a Mage: the Awakening game, which is explicitly gnostic. Problem is that the Seers of the Throne antagonists are painted as the unapologetic snitch or prison guard for the Exarchs overseeing the spiritual jail of the Fallen World, happily trading service and worship for temporal power. In essence, they aren't the Rosenbergs or Alger Hiss (the true believers of the other philosophy), they're the Aldrich Ames (whose services were bought with money). So it's hard to have a revelatory-experience-based antagonist, who just might be right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T12:49:59-08:00","id":1019373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019344#post1019344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the Marauders can arguably be the psychopaths of the awakened world, the Nephandi are the sociopaths, the sadists, and the extremists.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't the Marauders be the schizophrenics, spectrum disorder and disassociatives? It seems more like the Nephandi are the psychopaths....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T12:57:41-08:00","id":1019380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019361#post1019361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are either carrying out their evil acts or they aren't. If they aren't, if as you suggested their destructive nihilism is just a rationalization by mages who can't understand them, then they can't help their associations. If they are, and their actions are real and befit whatever enlightenment they think they have, then their associations are intentional (if inscrutable). Changing their end goal doesn't help much, because even their actions don't have to match up with any plan we can fathom.<br /> <br /> There could be, of course. Pain and suffering could be their lures to draw other destructive entities in. They could also be trying to alter the nature of the consensus by driving everyone to desire annihilation. But there doesn't have to be a rational rationale.</div> </div> </div> </div>New ways to shout and kill and revel and enjoy ourselves and all the world aflame in a holocaust of ecstasy and freedom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T13:03:46-08:00","id":1019383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019373#post1019373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't the Marauders be the schizophrenics, spectrum disorder and disassociatives? It seems more like the Nephandi are the psychopaths....</div> </div> </div> </div>As well. Psychopathy is an inability to distinguish between right and wrong due to insanity.<br /> This could fit either mould.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T14:52:04-08:00","id":1019433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019354#post1019354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That ratio was only because so many of them were in the Umbra when the Avatar Storm hit. Unless you're running a game set in the early millennium, the chances are the number of awakened people on earth has expanded quite a bit.<br /> <br /> Let's not forget, however, that even with numbers that low, 1 mage can out perform an entire group of sorcerers with very little trouble. Sorcerers run out of Willpower pretty frequently, and can sometimes need a few days to recover from larger rituals, Mages have no such limit. Sure they may have to be careful of paradox, but if their effects are subtle enough it barely matters. If a Tradition or Technocratic mage becomes aware of a Nephandic group of sorcerors, it won't be too difficult to find them, round them up, and end them without too much trouble as their powers or tech will be far and above anything the sorcerer would be capable of.<br /> <br /> Awakened mages, on therefor a much grander prize. Their potency is much greater, their abilities require much less time and are a heck of a lot more effective. But their does lie one other great incentives to recruit awakened mages. Being able to fight against the Tradition and Technocratic forces which seek to end their plans. This doesn't just work to match like with like fire power, it also allows a foothold for further corruption. What better way to tear down against the enemy, than having the enemy convert to ally?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never found Sorcerers to have much problem shutting down Mages. They have superior counterspells, and they do not depend on magic for killing. Now, five Sorcerers will probably go down against five Mages fairly quickly. However, five Infernal Sorcerers, with one of them having ten dice in the Countermagic Demonic Investment, will do horrible things to normal Mages.<br /> <br /> Though it is a matter of subtlety. Will PCs suspect Infernal Sorcerers when they find out that the town exploded in distrust and acrimony because men were cheating on their wives with teenage girls? Probably not, especially if the teenage girls do not flaunt their Infernal powers.<br /> <br /> And how many Mages can there be before Reality crumbles? 1:100,000 gives them comparable numbers to Fera, Kindred, and Kuei-jin. Unless cWoD was Mage and Friends, I doubt there are more Mages than Kindred, especially since Kindred can always make more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 12-19-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T14:53:20-08:00","id":1019435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019383#post1019383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As well. Psychopathy is an inability to distinguish between right and wrong due to insanity.<br /> This could fit either mould.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, let's not forget that the Bai Dai plan for achieving the Marauders' overall goals involved pruning the world's population back to pre-Medieval levels in order to weaken consensual reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T18:58:13-08:00","id":1019553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019383#post1019383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As well. Psychopathy is an inability to distinguish between right and wrong due to insanity.<br /> This could fit either mould.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically then, most Nephandi aren't psychopaths using your definition, as they clearly know the difference between &quot;right&quot; and &quot;wrong&quot; and choose to do &quot;wrong&quot;. Not that that makes them, as keeps getting put forward, nonsense. That's exactly how &quot;intent&quot; works in any criminal wrongdoing beyond criminal negligence. And lots and lots and lots of people are choosing to do &quot;wrong&quot; all the time. Why should mages be any different? It's the method and the scale.<br /> <br /> Ya... that makes Nephandi little more than &quot;reality criminals&quot;. So all the wailing and moaning and attempts to make them seem ultra-cool in a quasi-Nietschean way is pretty much just the same as being an apologist for any other perpetrator of reprehensible criminal acts. But, if the proverbial shoe fits....<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't make Marauders psychopaths. Or, at least, they don't have to be and typically aren't. The inability to distinguish right from wrong is not the same thing as the inability to distinguish what is real from what isn't. (Or what wouldn't be real if the person in question didn't redefine reality by fiat.) You can have Marauders who are psychopaths or sociopaths, but they are all disassociative to one degree or another., as their signature &quot;bit' is coming at &quot;normal&quot; reality from some different angle. <br /> <br /> A decent example from Intro to Criminal Law - If a schizoid person who believes they talk to Jesus and Jesus says &quot;Light that porn store on fire&quot; and then the schizoid person does... That's a crime (e.g. a &quot;wrong&quot; thing to do), because, despite the &quot;talking to Jesus&quot; part, he knew that lighting a building, particularly a building with people in it, is &quot;wrong&quot;. He's definitely not a psychopath. He's schizoid (and off his meds). And he's criminally liable for his actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T19:24:26-08:00","id":1019567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019553#post1019553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically then, most Nephandi aren't psychopaths using your definition, as they clearly know the difference between &amp;quot;right&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;wrong&amp;quot; and choose to do &amp;quot;wrong&amp;quot;. Not that that makes them, as keeps getting put forward, nonsense. That's exactly how &amp;quot;intent&amp;quot; works in any criminal wrongdoing beyond criminal negligence. And lots and lots and lots of people are choosing to do &amp;quot;wrong&amp;quot; all the time. Why should mages be any different? It's the method and the scale.<br /> <br /> Ya... that makes Nephandi little more than &amp;quot;reality criminals&amp;quot;. So all the wailing and moaning and attempts to make them seem ultra-cool in a quasi-Nietschean way is pretty much just the same as being an apologist for any other perpetrator of reprehensible criminal acts. But, if the proverbial shoe fits....<br /> <br /> However, that doesn't make Marauders psychopaths. Or, at least, they don't have to be and typically aren't. The inability to distinguish right from wrong is not the same thing as the inability to distinguish what is real from what isn't. (Or what wouldn't be real if the person in question didn't redefine reality by fiat.) You can have Marauders who are psychopaths or sociopaths, but they are all disassociative to one degree or another., as their signature &amp;quot;bit' is coming at &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; reality from some different angle. <br /> <br /> A decent example from Intro to Criminal Law - If a schizoid person who believes they talk to Jesus and Jesus says &amp;quot;Light that porn store on fire&amp;quot; and then the schizoid person does... That's a crime (e.g. a &amp;quot;wrong&amp;quot; thing to do), because, despite the &amp;quot;talking to Jesus&amp;quot; part, he knew that lighting a building, particularly a building with people in it, is &amp;quot;wrong&amp;quot;. He's definitely not a psychopath. He's schizoid (and off his meds). And he's criminally liable for his actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. That works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:24:09-08:00","id":1019708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019553#post1019553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ya... that makes Nephandi little more than &quot;reality criminals&quot;. So all the wailing and moaning and attempts to make them seem ultra-cool in a quasi-Nietschean way is pretty much just the same as being an apologist for any other perpetrator of reprehensible criminal acts. But, if the proverbial shoe fits...</div> </div> </div> </div>These attempts only happen because nephandi are cohesive, organized, have an hierarchy and are apparently rational actors in the ascension war. Thus I as a player am baffled by the lack of rational justifications or reasons for their objectives. What they see in the cauls that lead them to act like they act? What they learnt from oblivion demons that they ended like this?<br /> School shooters, serial killers, rapists are lonely people with mental illness, not an organization with an agenda. Mafia, criminal organizations, militant groups are &quot;evil&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; as long as they are marginalized, excluded or working illegally. Nephandi are none of these things.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7219-visigoth","name":"visigoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:48:43-08:00","id":1019712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019383#post1019383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As well. Psychopathy is an inability to distinguish between right and wrong due to insanity.<br /> This could fit either mould.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what psychopathy is. There's a lot of literature on just what it is. It's <i>not</i> insanity and it's <i>not</i> an inability to distinguish right from wrong. I strongly recommend pretty much anything by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_D._Hare\" target=\"_blank\">Robert D. Hare</a> if you want to be informed on the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:51:52-08:00","id":1019715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019553#post1019553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A decent example from Intro to Criminal Law - If a schizoid person who believes they talk to Jesus and Jesus says &quot;Light that porn store on fire&quot; and then the schizoid person does... That's a crime (e.g. a &quot;wrong&quot; thing to do), because, despite the &quot;talking to Jesus&quot; part, he knew that lighting a building, particularly a building with people in it, is &quot;wrong&quot;. He's definitely not a psychopath. He's schizoid (and off his meds). And he's criminally liable for his actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>A schizoid person doesn't experience psychosis. ITYM &quot;schizophrenic&quot; as well as possibly &quot;schizoaffective&quot; or &quot;schizotypal.&quot; Schizoid personality disorder is mostly just about not forming attachments to other people and preferring one's own company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T04:54:43-08:00","id":1019718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019433#post1019433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have never found Sorcerers to have much problem shutting down Mages. They have superior counterspells, and they do not depend on magic for killing. Now, five Sorcerers will probably go down against five Mages fairly quickly. However, five Infernal Sorcerers, with one of them having ten dice in the Countermagic Demonic Investment, will do horrible things to normal Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is very easy for STs to minimax opposition to easily defeat player characters. What's challenging is to give them a tough fight without just overwhelming them. Based on this and comments elsewhere about blowing players up with paradox it sounds like you run an exceedingly lethal game. I guess that's fine if your players are fine with it, but I've found it's a good way to develop high player turnover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019433#post1019433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how many Mages can there be before Reality crumbles? 1:100,000 gives them comparable numbers to Fera, Kindred, and Kuei-jin. Unless cWoD was Mage and Friends, I doubt there are more Mages than Kindred, especially since Kindred can always make more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1:100,000 number is genuinely too low, and I wouldn't expect any ST to hold to it when the answer is &quot;as many mages as you need for your game.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019346#post1019346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it worthwhile for a Demon Lord to invest in Nephandi? Given the rarity of Mages (1:100,000 in Revised), Nephandi are probably no more than 5% of them (1:2,000,000), I think that Demon Lords would get more bang for their buck converting angst ridden teenagers into Infernal Sorcerers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because nephandi can form groups just as easily as PCs can. They're as rare or as common as you need them to be. You shouldn't be designing your NPCs as if you were filling a quota.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019346#post1019346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Demon Lords would enter the dreams of the abused teenage girls, offer them some lesser powers in exchange for minor violations (consensual sex with dozens of adult men, dealing drugs at high school, desecration of churches, etc) and, when they high on easy power, offer them a soul pact for even greater power. Demon Lords could use a group of Infernal Sorcerer abused teenagr girls to destroy the entire social fabric of a small town by seducing adult men and revealing every dirty little secret of the town. When the town starts to burn, the Demon Lords would have them change their names and relocate to another small town, where they would recruit more abused teenage girls so they could destroy that town even faster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, there you go with the &quot;sex with underaged children&quot; theme again. Surely there are much better ways to communicate nastiness than pedophilia or hebephilia. You always go straight for this, though, even though it is creepy as hell. If an ST pulled this in a game I was playing, I'd quit and warn pretty much everyone to avoid him forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-20-2016, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T05:23:06-08:00","id":1019724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019708#post1019708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These attempts only happen because nephandi are cohesive, organized, have an hierarchy and are apparently rational actors in the ascension war. Thus I as a player am baffled by the lack of rational justifications or reasons for their objectives. What they see in the cauls that lead them to act like they act? What they learnt from oblivion demons that they ended like this?<br /> School shooters, serial killers, rapists are lonely people with mental illness, not an organization with an agenda. Mafia, criminal organizations, militant groups are &quot;evil&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; as long as they are marginalized, excluded or working illegally. Nephandi are none of these things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's an odd bit of reasoning that usually crops up where the Nephandi are concerned. We know they have a coherent ideology because they are so good at working together. We know they are cohesive and well organized because they are so good at meeting their goals. And we know they have coherent goals because they spring from a common ideology. I'm simplifying to underscore the circular reasoning, of course, but my point is we often ascribe more rationality and capability to the Nephandi than they deserve.<br /> <br /> The heart of the problem is this assumption that the Nephandi have intricate and well thought out goals. I don't think they do. Instead, they have very broad and general goals, like causing pain, destabilization, corruption, and despair. Those goals are easy to meet; the Nephandi could spend more time fighting each other than the rest of the world and they'd still be able to say they achieved something. Since others of them can use that pain, destabilization, corruption, or despair to power their own works, it might even be a valid claim. It's not a complicated plan though, and it doesn't require much organization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T06:04:28-08:00","id":1019734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019724#post1019724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's an odd bit of reasoning that usually crops up where the Nephandi are concerned. We know they have a coherent ideology because they are so good at working together. We know they are cohesive and well organized because they are so good at meeting their goals. And we know they have coherent goals because they spring from a common ideology. I'm simplifying to underscore the circular reasoning, of course, but my point is we often ascribe more rationality and capability to the Nephandi than they deserve.<br /> <br /> The heart of the problem is this assumption that the Nephandi have intricate and well thought out goals. I don't think they do. Instead, they have very broad and general goals, like causing pain, destabilization, corruption, and despair. Those goals are easy to meet; the Nephandi could spend more time fighting each other than the rest of the world and they'd still be able to say they achieved something. Since others of them can use that pain, destabilization, corruption, or despair to power their own works, it might even be a valid claim. It's not a complicated plan though, and it doesn't require much organization.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. I think the impression of stability and having an intricate plan is actually one of the weapons they use. In reality they are as disorganised as any other mage, prone to argument and infighting. But because there is no limit to the lengths they will go to to prove a point, there is always the threat that if they go too far in the debate, they may end up killed. Generally speaking the lower ranks will either shut up and go along with the stronger members, or prepare to prove themselves worthy of having an outspoken opinion on threat of death.<br /> <br /> But from the outside perspective, anything they do badly can contribute to encouraging the demise of the world, even being killed by the hands of a mage, since not even the euthanatos accept killing solely as a means to an end. No matter what happens, they can turn around and taunt their adversary with a quick &quot;Thank you, you've served my plan very well&quot;, and let their own psychology do the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T08:29:24-08:00","id":1019784,"title":"","content":"Though I think that most Nephandi would rather live to corrupt another day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T09:21:37-08:00","id":1019813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019708#post1019708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These attempts only happen because nephandi are cohesive, organized, have an hierarchy and are apparently rational actors in the ascension war. Thus I as a player am baffled by the lack of rational justifications or reasons for their objectives. What they see in the cauls that lead them to act like they act? What they learnt from oblivion demons that they ended like this?<br /> School shooters, serial killers, rapists are lonely people with mental illness, not an organization with an agenda. Mafia, criminal organizations, militant groups are &quot;evil&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; as long as they are marginalized, excluded or working illegally. Nephandi are none of these things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not, strictly speaking, true. Remorseless killers of all sorts are vital parts of many different organizations. As are sociopaths who are more than happy to watch people suffer. Even legitimized sexual assault can be handled on a scale so industrial it becomes almost mundane. Some organizations have no problems with all of the above and more in the way of being completely antisocial as a part of their functionality. Lots of bad actors are completely rational, including, even especially, those who work (well) in groups.<br /> <br /> In addition, there are definitely lone gunman-style Nephandi out there who are definitely more like mass or serial killers (or mass serial killer, since one is dependent on the body count and the other on the number of incidents, it's more than possible to be both). And some organized Nephandi are more than happy to utilize such in whatever fashion is most productive (let 'em go and watch the ruin, direct their path, bring them in but let them remain autonomous to a degree, bring them in and keep them on a short leash, give them a seat at the table, etc.)<br /> <br /> People who do bad things aren't always excluded or marginalized. In fact, they can be integral to society or even achieve a power position (or, they may have or maintain the power position by being the kind of people who do bad things). Of course, they can also be marginalized and insular as well. But they don't have to be. <br /> <br /> I am just not seeing anything so super special about Nephandi that makes them that much different from mundane folks who choose similar paths. I know, I know... the Cauls.... But whatever that might mean, the folks spat out seem to be humans. Just antisocial humans with seriously bad attitudes. Maybe all the Cauls do is just strip away the fundamental social programming that has to do with having issues being a jerk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T12:50:37-08:00","id":1019932,"title":"","content":"I agree with Ramnesis and Saikou. The Intricacy of a plan isn't necessarily relevant to how well it goes off (indeed, there's something to be said of having too many moving parts, because it creates more places where the mechanism could fail). Even a single layer of obfuscation is enough to cause damage, which is one of the main things Nephandi as a group work for.<br /> <br /> Send a package in the mail to a random person who is down on their luck. It contains a stack of money and instructions to go to a certain house in the city and leave a note enclosed in the package. With the cash (and maybe a little Mind enchantment on the note to nudge the person towards compliance), the patsy is told that they can continue receiving rewards for further &quot;errands&quot;. The stooge has no idea they are helping facilitate a campaign of psychological warfare against someone by doing their seemingly innocuous tasks. Psychological warfare that could be working to isolate a Mage from their fellow Awakened, or making a Technocrat agent doubt their sanity, or make a common office worker have a nervous breakdown (which may or may not result in them taking a shotgun to work one day). If the patsy just so happens to already be a drug addict, who suddenly has a steady supply of cash to feed their habit for very little work, all's the better as far as their dark manipulator is concerned. They can do whatever it is they want to do, and further ruin a poor bystander's life in the process.<br /> <br /> The best part being that, even if the target somehow tracks things back to the patsy, the latter has no idea who they work for. Not even Mind or Time magick helps illuminate the issue, since the Nephandus was no where near their puppet. If the Nephandus is unnecessarily paranoid, they could create a second layer of obfuscation by having all the letters be copies transcribed verbatum by a person who doesn't understand the language, and who also never met their &quot;client&quot;. But, again, this isn't really necessary.<br /> <br /> And this is when you're getting a little complicated. I definitely overthought that plan. A Nephandus could get the same effect by arranging for a mental patient to escape confinement, and appear to them as a figure from their delusions, telling them to kill the whores or whatever. Most Mages who even bother to investigate a random serial killer would need to make a huge leap in logic to assume the guy is being manipulated, instead of just obeying the voices in their head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 12-20-2016, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T13:47:35-08:00","id":1019950,"title":"","content":"What Bluecho just stated definitely struck a chord with me.<br /> <br /> Mages spend a lot of time concerned with mage things. They aren't suposed to hang around in one place and get to know a setting. They are supposed to be on life/visionquests understanding the is of is and all those what's and wheretofor's. <br /> <br /> Which means Nephandi can nudge the world merrily off to Hell by just spending their efforts on normal mundane folks. Most mages won't even notice a serial killer unless there is something exceptional or apparently supernatural about it. And that's even if they are around enough to notice something that's mostly on the local news. Even the Union has normal people to handle normal people, even abnormal normal people. Like, say, the FBI.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T14:25:25-08:00","id":1019970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019932#post1019932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is when you're getting a little complicated. I definitely overthought that plan. A Nephandus could get the same effect by arranging for a mental patient to escape confinement, and appear to them as a figure from their delusions, telling them to kill the whores or whatever. Most Mages who even bother to investigate a random serial killer would need to make a huge leap in logic to assume the guy is being manipulated, instead of just obeying the voices in their head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although it wouldn't be a very big leap in logic at all to realize that violent crime of that nature is very rare from mentally ill people and that mentally ill people are much more likely to be victims of violence than perpetrators.<br /> <br /> That is to say what you describe here is a huge red flag to me, and that's not a huge leap in logic. That's just how things work.<br /> <br /> Like, you'd only really fool people who already believe that delusions and hallucinations commonly lead people to violence, and holding such a belief means being extremely ignorant about psychology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T14:31:41-08:00","id":1019974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019950#post1019950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Bluecho just stated definitely struck a chord with me.<br /> <br /> Mages spend a lot of time concerned with mage things. They aren't suposed to hang around in one place and get to know a setting. They are supposed to be on life/visionquests understanding the is of is and all those what's and wheretofor's.<br /> <br /> Which means Nephandi can nudge the world merrily off to Hell by just spending their efforts on normal mundane folks. Most mages won't even notice a serial killer unless there is something exceptional or apparently supernatural about it. And that's even if they are around enough to notice something that's mostly on the local news. Even the Union has normal people to handle normal people, even abnormal normal people. Like, say, the FBI.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, domestic threats on this level would mostly be the interest of the Technocracy, especially the NWO run FBI and the Syndicate run/influenced local police.<br /> <br /> That being said, I don't think all mages are nomads. Mages are people like anyone else. If they've got a job, a family, or even a prominent position in the local Chantry, there's no reason for them to go gallivanting of into adventure when their studies/research/practice/whatever is progressing quite nicely where they are.<br /> <br /> Choristers may leave in a monastry near a village for several years of their life. Hermetics could spend decades in university type settings teaching and researching. An ecstatic might have a theatre or a bar to keep running.<br /> <br /> Also, there are lots of mages who keep involved with sleepers. Some do it out of a sense of duty, others perhaps because they fear losing their humanity. There are entire factions such as House Jerbiton of the Hermetics, or the Moon Seekers of the Verbena who specifically emphasise the importance of keeping in touch with Sleeper Society. Any of these groups would be people the nephandi would have to navigate around in order to lay their traps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T14:38:41-08:00","id":1019979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019970#post1019970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although it wouldn't be a very big leap in logic at all to realize that violent crime of that nature is very rare from mentally ill people and that mentally ill people are much more likely to be victims of violence than perpetrators.<br /> <br /> That is to say what you describe here is a huge red flag to me, and that's not a huge leap in logic. That's just how things work.<br /> <br /> Like, you'd only really fool people who already believe that delusions and hallucinations commonly lead people to violence, and holding such a belief means being extremely ignorant about psychology.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The sad thing is that what's true doesn't really matter. What people believe is much stronger.<br /> <br /> If the population think that schizophrenia is a disease which causes violent behaviour and can lead people to become murderers, then people are going to make those logical links. This sort of stuff is perpetuated by the mainstream media, from Crime shows like Criminal Minds and CSI, to movies like Psycho and Halloween.<br /> <br /> People have it in their minds still to this day that Crazed Killers who escape from the nearby asylum are likely to come at you with a knife. It doesn't matter if it's demonstrably false, people believe it, and that's all the nephandi needs to make this work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T14:52:12-08:00","id":1019987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019970#post1019970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although it wouldn't be a very big leap in logic at all to realize that violent crime of that nature is very rare from mentally ill people and that mentally ill people are much more likely to be victims of violence than perpetrators.<br /> <br /> That is to say what you describe here is a huge red flag to me, and that's not a huge leap in logic. That's just how things work.<br /> <br /> Like, you'd only really fool people who already believe that delusions and hallucinations commonly lead people to violence, and holding such a belief means being extremely ignorant about psychology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you have to be extremely ignorant. I think the media and popular culture feed that myth enough that a fair amount of people believe it. This being World of Darkness, I don't see said myths being less commonly believed than in real life. I certainly agree with the facts you stated. But not with the idea that it is a commonly held belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T16:25:23-08:00","id":1020040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019979#post1019979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The sad thing is that what's true doesn't really matter. What people believe is much stronger.<br /> <br /> If the population think that schizophrenia is a disease which causes violent behaviour and can lead people to become murderers, then people are going to make those logical links. This sort of stuff is perpetuated by the mainstream media, from Crime shows like Criminal Minds and CSI, to movies like Psycho and Halloween.<br /> <br /> People have it in their minds still to this day that Crazed Killers who escape from the nearby asylum are likely to come at you with a knife. It doesn't matter if it's demonstrably false, people believe it, and that's all the nephandi needs to make this work.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019987#post1019987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you have to be extremely ignorant. I think the media and popular culture feed that myth enough that a fair amount of people believe it. This being World of Darkness, I don't see said myths being less commonly believed than in real life. I certainly agree with the facts you stated. But not with the idea that it is a commonly held belief.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought we were talking about mages, though. If there's a plague of schizophrenic murderers (that's even assuming they obey the command to kill - even schizophrenic people with command hallucinations aren't robots who do everything the voices tell them to do) it should stand out to <i>mages</i> who pay attention to <i>weird shit</i> happening in their area.<br /> <br /> I don't expect any rational human being who is not in some way supernatural to conclude: Rash of murders by schizophrenic patients? MAGIC. Because that'd be ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T17:31:31-08:00","id":1020074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019974#post1019974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, domestic threats on this level would mostly be the interest of the Technocracy, especially the NWO run FBI and the Syndicate run/influenced local police.<br /> <br /> That being said, I don't think all mages are nomads. Mages are people like anyone else. If they've got a job, a family, or even a prominent position in the local Chantry, there's no reason for them to go gallivanting of into adventure when their studies/research/practice/whatever is progressing quite nicely where they are.<br /> <br /> Choristers may leave in a monastry near a village for several years of their life. Hermetics could spend decades in university type settings teaching and researching. An ecstatic might have a theatre or a bar to keep running.<br /> <br /> Also, there are lots of mages who keep involved with sleepers. Some do it out of a sense of duty, others perhaps because they fear losing their humanity. There are entire factions such as House Jerbiton of the Hermetics, or the Moon Seekers of the Verbena who specifically emphasise the importance of keeping in touch with Sleeper Society. Any of these groups would be people the nephandi would have to navigate around in order to lay their traps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that Phil Brucato has specifically said that Mage is not designed or intended to be a setting based game. Period. No questions. It's all about the plot, man. The JOURNEY. The development of the spirit and the soul. Which, apparently, cannot occur if you do not keep physically moving from place to place. <br /> <br /> Please make sure to ignore all those Backgrounds that only really work well (or at all) if the characters actually live somewhere consistently. (Or make sure that there's always Correspondence 3 and a handy familiar to eat all the Dox from the rampant teleportation back to the Sanctum, Node, your Ally's house so you can hold up your end of the relationships, whatever)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T17:53:22-08:00","id":1020083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020040#post1020040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought we were talking about mages, though. If there's a plague of schizophrenic murderers (that's even assuming they obey the command to kill - even schizophrenic people with command hallucinations aren't robots who do everything the voices tell them to do) it should stand out to <i>mages</i> who pay attention to <i>weird shit</i> happening in their area.<br /> <br /> I don't expect any rational human being who is not in some way supernatural to conclude: Rash of murders by schizophrenic patients? MAGIC. Because that'd be ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are talking about mages. My point being, I think mages can be equally uneducated and ignorant when it comes to psychology. My perception being, even a mage would probably write off hearing about some murders by a 'crazy' person as either media hype or what have you. Unless there was a clearly occult cause showing or perhaps mind based, I'm not sure why a mage would be especially intuitive about it. I doubt mages come about theories to say, the Zodiac Killer or what have you. Granted, the Zodiac Killer might not have been clinically insane, but that's the impression pop-culture tries to give. I think they'd be inundated by that sort of thing to a similar degree. <br /> <br /> Now if it was a <i>plague</i> of <i>murderers</i> all focused around one insane asylum, maybe. But that's just sloppy in general and doesn't have the same bearing as 'crazy serial killer equals corrupted patient via Barabi,' which seemed more of the point of discussion. We were talking about just one patient in an area doing one specific crime at the time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T18:23:29-08:00","id":1020093,"title":"","content":"While serial murderers are horrific, the Nephandi do not really need to encourage them. The Nephandi would be involved ruining the lives of everyone around them and, quite frankly, serial murder is just one part of the crap pile that the Nephandi will be pursuing. I imagine that more Nephandi will be involved in pyramid schemes that destroy the pension funds of tens of thousands of people, causing suffering to tens of thousands of families, than they will be encouraging serial killers. The pyramid schemes also have an added benefit of disrupting the economic machinery that the Technocracy depends on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T18:26:32-08:00","id":1020096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020083#post1020083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are talking about mages. My point being, I think mages can be equally uneducated and ignorant when it comes to psychology. My perception being, even a mage would probably write off hearing about some murders by a 'crazy' person as either media hype or what have you. Unless there was a clearly occult cause showing or perhaps mind based, I'm not sure why a mage would be especially intuitive about it. I doubt mages come about theories to say, the Zodiac Killer or what have you. Granted, the Zodiac Killer might not have been clinically insane, but that's the impression pop-culture tries to give. I think they'd be inundated by that sort of thing to a similar degree.<br /> <br /> Now if it was a <i>plague</i> of <i>murderers</i> all focused around one insane asylum, maybe. But that's just sloppy in general and doesn't have the same bearing as 'crazy serial killer equals corrupted patient via Barabi,' which seemed more of the point of discussion. We were talking about just one patient in an area doing one specific crime at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>If mages aren't going to figure out the nephandi are up to something, why have nephandi in the first place? It's a waste of time if it's not a plot hook.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I would think that mages have a better chance of being informed about such things (Academics and Medicine are skills in M20, after all).<br /> <br /> Also, I'd argue that a nephandi busting a schizophrenic out and trying to convince them to kill kill kill is mostly a waste of the nephandi's time. There are better ways to spread discord, chaos, and misery that would make far more interesting story hooks for player character mages to deal with.<br /> <br /> And...that's pretty much all I have to say. I'm not really interested in going back and forth on why nephandi are too clever to be caught - that's a waste of my time and yours.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T18:39:33-08:00","id":1020102,"title":"","content":"Nephandi should be careful enough not to directly associate with the mortals who do the dirty work (much like traditional Mafia bosses used capos as intermediaries for anything nasty). I can imagine a Nephandi running a pyramid scheme with the eventual intention to destroy the retirements of tens of thousands of families and investing the money generated by the pyramid scheme in arms running, drug smuggling, human trafficking, etc. Each dollar taken from the clean investment fund can make five soiled dollars in the criminal underworld through spreading pain and suffering. Catching a smart Nephandi should be like catching a Mafia Don, you get them on the details they were too overconfident to fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T18:52:47-08:00","id":1020114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020096#post1020096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If mages aren't going to figure out the nephandi are up to something, why have nephandi in the first place? It's a waste of time if it's not a plot hook.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I would think that mages have a better chance of being informed about such things (Academics and Medicine are skills in M20, after all).<br /> <br /> Also, I'd argue that a nephandi busting a schizophrenic out and trying to convince them to kill kill kill is mostly a waste of the nephandi's time. There are better ways to spread discord, chaos, and misery that would make far more interesting story hooks for player character mages to deal with.<br /> <br /> And...that's pretty much all I have to say. I'm not really interested in going back and forth on why nephandi are too clever to be caught - that's a waste of my time and yours.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point wasn't necessarily that Nephandi are too clever to be caught. I just found the characterization of Mages not being as prone to buying into certain myths/misconceptions as normal people do to be unfair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:11:43-08:00","id":1020298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020114#post1020114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point wasn't necessarily that Nephandi are too clever to be caught. I just found the characterization of Mages not being as prone to buying into certain myths/misconceptions as normal people do to be unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if mages are just as prone as normal people to buying into myths and misconceptions (something I think is definitely untrue) then the Nephandi is by definition too clever to be caught. One thing has the other as a consequence.<br /> <br /> I mean the scenario itself is blatantly ridiculous - just because someone hears voices doesn't mean they'll obey them. Just because someone hears voices doesn't mean they'll believe the nephandi's simulation of said voice to actually be that voice. Schizophrenia doesn't turn people into programmable robots and it is very easy to get them to distrust what you're saying.<br /> <br /> Nephandi who want to actually achieve evil ends would seek other means to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:15:03-08:00","id":1020301,"title":"","content":"Edit: Nevermind, I have better ways to spend my time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-21-2016, 08:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:25:23-08:00","id":1020307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020083#post1020083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are talking about mages. My point being, I think mages can be equally uneducated and ignorant when it comes to psychology. My perception being, even a mage would probably write off hearing about some murders by a 'crazy' person as either media hype or what have you. Unless there was a clearly occult cause showing or perhaps mind based, I'm not sure why a mage would be especially intuitive about it. I doubt mages come about theories to say, the Zodiac Killer or what have you. Granted, the Zodiac Killer might not have been clinically insane, but that's the impression pop-culture tries to give. I think they'd be inundated by that sort of thing to a similar degree.<br /> <br /> Now if it was a <i>plague</i> of <i>murderers</i> all focused around one insane asylum, maybe. But that's just sloppy in general and doesn't have the same bearing as 'crazy serial killer equals corrupted patient via Barabi,' which seemed more of the point of discussion. We were talking about just one patient in an area doing one specific crime at the time.was</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree wholeheartedly with your point, but I think that, probably the Zodiac Killer might represent one of the cases that WOULD draw the attention of mages. The killings were so overtly occult in nature and there is still the perception (and reality) of mystery around them. That's in opposition to John Wayne Gacy or Jeffrey Dahmer or Ted Bundy or the like. Who seem much more mundane overall. Even only one victim might interest mages, depending on the circumstances, like, say, the girls who murdered in the name of the Slenderman. <br /> <br /> The point being that a Nephandi with the right Spheres could probably create a bunch of Bundys and Dahmers and set them loose (Murder Academy?) and it probably wouldn't ping the radar of mages at all unless, say, a victim was a personal friend. I doubt it would even register for the Union. The NWO seems like the only part heavily implicated and, without some kind of indication of supernatural involvement, they have the FBI, et al. to do that sort of thing for them. They have much bigger fish to fry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:29:17-08:00","id":1020310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020298#post1020298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if mages are just as prone as normal people to buying into myths and misconceptions (something I think is definitely untrue) then the Nephandi is by definition too clever to be caught. One thing has the other as a consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really. As you have said, they only really serve as a plot point or a means to an end. Is all a Nephandi doing is going city to city influencing a select few mentally ill patients to become serial killers with leaving any evidence/influence? Probably not for numerous reasons. I'd even say the first sentence is a mischaracterization of what I'm getting at. I'm not even saying Mages are just as prone to buying into myths and misconceptions period. Certainly their exposure would allow them more insight into certain things. I don't see psychology as being one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean the scenario itself is blatantly ridiculous - just because someone hears voices doesn't mean they'll obey them. Just because someone hears voices doesn't mean they'll believe the nephandi's simulation of said voice to actually be that voice. Schizophrenia doesn't turn people into programmable robots and it is very easy to get them to distrust what you're saying.<br /> <br /> Nephandi who want to actually achieve evil ends would seek other means to do so. </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily even disagree with any of this. But again, it sort of misses the only point I had. I'm not saying, 'this is what Nephandi do as their go to evil. And Mages are too slow to catch on' Just that I don't see a typical mage reacting with the mindset, 'serial killer with mental illness? Something isn't right.' I don't think the misconception of mentally ill people being violent, which is indeed a problematic misconception in media, is something Mages don't share to the point that any who don't think the above are &quot;extremely ignorant about psychology.&quot; Or, if we really need to get into the semantics, I think the general characterization of many Mages as not being ignorant about certain points of psychology to be unrealistic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020307#post1020307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree wholeheartedly with your point, but I think that, probably the Zodiac Killer might represent one of the cases that WOULD draw the attention of mages. The killings were so overtly occult in nature and there is still the perception (and reality) of mystery around them. That's in opposition to John Wayne Gacy or Jeffrey Dahmer or Ted Bundy or the like. Who seem much more mundane overall. Even only one victim might interest mages, depending on the circumstances, like, say, the girls who murdered in the name of the Slenderman.<br /> <br /> The point being that a Nephandi with the right Spheres could probably create a bunch of Bundys and Dahmers and set them loose (Murder Academy?) and it probably wouldn't ping the radar of mages at all unless, say, a victim was a personal friend. I doubt it would even register for the Union. The NWO seems like the only part heavily implicated and, without some kind of indication of supernatural involvement, they have the FBI, et al. to do that sort of thing for them. They have much bigger fish to fry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I could have picked a better example. But yeah, the main thought was 'suspect of serial murders is mentally ill' wouldn't be an intrinsic link to 'mentally ill person was probably, or even likely to be a pawn of a Nephandi.' That does seem like a leap. Like, I think Dahmer had some illness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 12-21-2016, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:38:00-08:00","id":1020316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020298#post1020298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But if mages are just as prone as normal people to buying into myths and misconceptions (something I think is definitely untrue) then the Nephandi is by definition too clever to be caught. One thing has the other as a consequence.<br /> <br /> I mean the scenario itself is blatantly ridiculous - just because someone hears voices doesn't mean they'll obey them. Just because someone hears voices doesn't mean they'll believe the nephandi's simulation of said voice to actually be that voice. Schizophrenia doesn't turn people into programmable robots and it is very easy to get them to distrust what you're saying.<br /> <br /> Nephandi who want to actually achieve evil ends would seek other means to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really weird &quot;all or nothing&quot; attitude, you know?<br /> <br /> Yes, not every mentally I'll person who hears voices will act on them, but some do because it's not just hearing them that the disease affects, it's believing them as well.<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, especially I Mage, all forms of myth can potentially be true.<br /> A mage that baulks at the idea of Fairies is just as foolish as mage that thinks computers have no place in mysticism. Mages are coloured by their beliefs and this gives way to misconceptions. Mages as a whole are not more understanding and able to pick truth from lies by proxy of being mages, otherwise there would be no ascension war.<br /> <br /> If a schizophrenic person awakens into a marauder state and what was once personal senses becomes manifest, who's to say they wouldn't be more suseptible to suggestion?<br /> <br /> Who's to say a mage wouldn't think the marauder was acting without influence?<br /> <br /> Also, not every nephandi's goal is identical. Perhaps this one wanted to make a point about mental illness, or had a vendetta against the hospital or a specific doctor. Or maybe he just really like psycho horror and wanted to make his own real life Haloween movie for fun.<br /> <br /> Nephandi are as verried as any other mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-21-2016, 08:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:49:17-08:00","id":1020322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020310#post1020310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, I could have picked a better example. But yeah, the main thought was 'suspect of serial murders is mentally ill' wouldn't be an intrinsic link to 'mentally ill person was probably, or even likely to be a pawn of a Nephandi.' That does seem like a leap. Like, I think Dahmer had some illness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say it would lead them straight to &quot;pawn of a Nephandi<i>.&quot;</i> I said it'd be suspicious, a red flag.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020316#post1020316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, not every mentally I'll person who hears voices will act on them, but some do because it's not just hearing them that the disease affects, it's believing them as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have experience talking to people who actually hear voices and: Not all mentally ill people who hear voices act on them. Not all mentally ill people who believe their voices are real act on them. Many refuse command hallucinations even as such hallucinations can cause significant distress. If someone finds that one of their voices is ordering them to kill they can still say &quot;no.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know about anosognosia (lack of insight/ability to understand that delusions and hallucinations aren't real) but I also know that how people respond to these voices, whether they think they're real or are aware they're hallucinating varies widely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020316#post1020316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the World of Darkness, especially I Mage, all forms of myth can potentially be true.<br /> A mage that baulks at the idea of Fairies is just as foolish as mage that thinks computers have no place in mysticism. Mages are coloured by their beliefs and this gives way to misconceptions. Mages as a whole are not more understanding and able to pick truth from lies by proxy of being mages, otherwise there would be no ascension war.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't really relevant. Mages possibly being better informed about things doesn't mean they can always pick truth from lies. You have a really weird &quot;all or nothing&quot; attitude, you know?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020316#post1020316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a schizophrenic person awakens into a marauder state and what was once personal senses becomes manifest, who's to say they wouldn't be more suseptible to suggestion?<br /> <br /> Who's to say a mage wouldn't think the marauder was acting without influence?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a nephandi who tries to influence a marauder is taking his life into his own hands. I also think a nephandi who does that might not be a problem for very long.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020316#post1020316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, not every nephandi's goal is identical. Perhaps this one wanted to make a point about mental illness, or had a vendetta against the hospital or a specific doctor. Or maybe he just really like psycho horror and wanted to make his own real life Haloween movie for fun.<br /> <br /> Nephandi are as verried as any other mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but one assumes they like to be effective at achieving their goals, and this is a rather ineffective way to achieve any goal except random mayhem. I imagine a nephandi who wants to harm mentally ill people is more likely to abuse those mentally ill people, probably in a hospital setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 12-21-2016, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T06:17:15-08:00","id":1020339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020322#post1020322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say it would lead them straight to &quot;pawn of a Nephandi<i>.&quot;</i> I said it'd be suspicious, a red flag.</div> </div> </div> </div> The phrases you used were, 'huge red flag, not a huge logical leap,' and ' you'd only really fool people who already believe that delusions and hallucinations commonly lead people to violence, and holding such a belief means being extremely ignorant about psychology.'<br /> <br /> The implication behind the last one being that Mages typically are not ignorant enough to not make a connection. If a murderer with claimed mental illness is a huge red flag, the Mage is more likely to waste his time more than anything. It just doesn't seem realistic to even say that much. I'd be hard pressed to imagine a scenario where a Mage hears about, say, James Holmes or David Berkowitz on the news, for other examples. And any huge red flags are waving at that. Again, especially in World of Darkness. If these things happen on occasion in real life, I'm not sure why isolated incidents here would be a big tell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T07:06:10-08:00","id":1020373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020322#post1020322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't say it would lead them straight to &amp;quot;pawn of a Nephandi<i>.&amp;quot;</i> I said it'd be suspicious, a red flag.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have experience talking to people who actually hear voices and: Not all mentally ill people who hear voices act on them. Not all mentally ill people who believe their voices are real act on them. Many refuse command hallucinations even as such hallucinations can cause significant distress. If someone finds that one of their voices is ordering them to kill they can still say &amp;quot;no.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I know about anosognosia (lack of insight/ability to understand that delusions and hallucinations aren't real) but I also know that how people respond to these voices, whether they think they're real or are aware they're hallucinating varies widely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This isn't really relevant. Mages possibly being better informed about things doesn't mean they can always pick truth from lies. You have a really weird &amp;quot;all or nothing&amp;quot; attitude, you know?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think a nephandi who tries to influence a marauder is taking his life into his own hands. I also think a nephandi who does that might not be a problem for very long.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, but one assumes they like to be effective at achieving their goals, and this is a rather ineffective way to achieve any goal except random mayhem. I imagine a nephandi who wants to harm mentally ill people is more likely to abuse those mentally ill people, probably in a hospital setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly are you trying to argue here?<br /> <br /> That there is no way any mental patient would act on their delusions?<br /> <br /> That no nephandi would take advantage of a vulnerable mentally ill person who has trouble telling real from senses?<br /> <br /> That no mage could possibly be fooled by an influenced mentally ill person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-21-2016, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:24:27-08:00","id":1020436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020373#post1020373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What exactly are you trying to argue here?<br /> <br /> That there is no way any mental patient would act on their delusions?<br /> <br /> That no nephandi would take advantage of a vulnerable mentally I'll person who has trouble telling real from senses?<br /> <br /> That no mage could possibly be fooled by an influenced mentally I'll person?</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of sums up what I've been meaning to say. No one is arguing that every mental patient is a violent killer who will do whatever their hallucinations tell them. But they do exist, in however low numbers. At this point, the problem turns into whether the Nephadus can find the &quot;right&quot; patient for their purposes. This is where the Nephandi's research skills and connections in the circles of psychiatry come into play. (I'll also be discussing the matter of mental illness in another post, for a different point of relevance).<br /> <br /> Further, no one is arguing that Mages aren't capable of seeing mental patients as the unwell people that they are, instead of all being violent killers. A Dreamspeaker shaman, for instance, might have plenty of personal experience with the mentally ill if they had a stint in a mental hospital, stemming from the nature of the spirit-focused Awakening. Or a Chorister who ministers to the poor and destitute, many of whom suffer mental illness.<br /> <br /> What we are arguing is that, again, this particular knowledge or understanding is not a given, even for the supposedly Enlightened. Mages are humans like everyone else, and not every human has the opportunity or the desire to learn about mental illness. For a good portion of the population - Mages included - the Truth of the matter lies outside their experience, at which point the only source of information they are likely familiar with is Media portrayals of them. Which, we can all agree, are not terribly accurate or favorable to the mentally ill. While Mages have the capacity to see things the way they are, they are just as able to be lead astray by lies, especially if they don't have a personal stake in accuracy. A Hermetic who basically lives in a university library has no reason to study psychology and mental health over subjects more pertinent to her own magickal development, let alone going out to interact with them.<br /> <br /> It comes down to which Mage characters would be around if a serial killer starts their &quot;work&quot;. If any of them &quot;know better&quot;, they could take an interest in the case. But if they don't &quot;know better&quot;, they only have popular conceptions of mental illness to go off of, and will react accordingly. Some will, indeed, dismiss the matter as &quot;crazies being crazy&quot;, and return to their own preoccupations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:51:35-08:00","id":1020453,"title":"","content":"Concerning further the matter of mentally ill patsies to Nephandic plots, I would like to point out that not everyone with a Delusion that can be exploited is Schizophrenic. Not all of them have hallucinations. Someone with Paranoid Delusions is otherwise in proper touch with their senses and thought processes, but has come to irregular conclusions about Reality.<br /> <br /> I say this not without a sense of irony, given the game we're talking about.<br /> <br /> Some may believe that someone is out to get them, or that &quot;They&quot; secretly control the world through bizarre means, for unknown purposes. That the world actually IS controlled by at least a couple of monolithic conspiracies can work in the favor of a Nephandic manipulator. As can the fact that, unlike the person suffering from hallucinations, does not have experience with voices that tell them to do horrible things (and therefore are not to be trusted or obeyed). The person with Paranoid Delusions believes in a certain view of the world, and that view can be exploited so long as the manipulator knows the delusion. (It's here that the Mind Sphere becomes very important, as a tool for reading thoughts and charting out what the person believes). <br /> <br /> The Nephandus could contact this poor person, claiming to be working for or against the shadowy conspiracy the person believes in. That the conspiracy is a conspiracy, and &quot;anyone could be watching, listening, or in on the plot&quot;, would be all the justification the patsy would need for why their new &quot;friend&quot; needs to minimize contact and limit traces that could come back to them. From there, it's a matter of telling the person what they want to hear, validating their beliefs, while introducing new ones. Then the Nephandus starts giving the person instructions, giving them hints on how they can help or hinder &quot;Them&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's important at this stage for the Nephandus, as with all pawns, to start the delusional person off small. Telling them to go out and kill is too much for anyone to expect from the average person (for a certain value of &quot;average&quot;, when paranoid conspiracy theories are concerned). They would resist. But if the tasks are small, manageable, and seemingly benign, the person would go along with it. Many of these could be nonsense tasks, assigned for no reason other than to get the pawn used to being a pawn, and to deepen their loyalty. Which each communication, however, the tasks become increasingly large...and increasingly immoral. Petty theft here, destruction of property there, knocking out electricity to this Technocrat Construct, burning down that Tradition magic shop. So long as the Nephandus can justify it, the pawn will grow willing to do worse and worse things. This is an established part of psychology: each task is an incremental compromise of their values, until they have been built up into doing just about anything.<br /> <br /> Eventually you have the patsy kidnapping innocent people, assured that, as they hold a gun to their victim's head, they are ultimately working to neutralize some puppet or another of &quot;Them&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's all before the Nephandus starts sending the pawn a few &quot;tools&quot; to help them out in the war. Charms, Trinkets, and minor Talismans that can increase their odds against the conspiracy. It shouldn't need to go that far, of course, unless the pawn is especially valuable. Magical or technomagical items, after all, can be traced back to their source. A lone gunman against the world, though, can be effective on his own, if fed the right &quot;intel&quot;. The best part being that he'll never betray his controller. Both because he knows nothing (and fully believes that this ignorance is justified, for the good of &quot;the mission&quot;), and because he thinks anyone who would want to stop or interrogate him is one of &quot;Them&quot;, and not to be helped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T16:26:03-08:00","id":1020698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019708#post1019708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These attempts only happen because nephandi are cohesive, organized, have an hierarchy and are apparently rational actors in the ascension war. Thus I as a player am baffled by the lack of rational justifications or reasons for their objectives. What they see in the cauls that lead them to act like they act? What they learnt from oblivion demons that they ended like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, those are the big questions aren't they? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Questions we all want to know the answers, but ones better left unanswered, to maintain some of the mystery and horror in an otherwise very detailed setting. What is on the other side of the Cauls that changes someone so profoundly? Where's Caine and Lilith and what they're doing? Who are the Aralu? things like that.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T07:33:11-08:00","id":1020874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think a nephandi who tries to influence a marauder is taking his life into his own hands. I also think a nephandi who does that might not be a problem for very long. </div> </div> </div>To put it mildly.<br /> <br /> Marauders will attack Nephandi on sight.<br /> As in, you present a room full of Things That Are A Problem For Marauders to one of them, and they will go for the Nephandi first. Always.<br /> <br /> And if you think Marauders are too confused or mad to know what Nephandi are, I reeeeeeeaaaaally suggest grabbing a copy of the Book Of Madness, First(!) Edition. It has a couple of facts and background on Marauders that were kept hush-hush in later writeups. Let's just say they are indeed a faction in the Ascension War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-22-2016, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T09:28:33-08:00","id":1020921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020874#post1020874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To put it mildly.<br /> <br /> Marauders will attack Nephandi on sight.<br /> As in, you present a room full of Things That Are A Problem For Marauders to one of them, and they will go for the Nephandi first. Always.<br /> <br /> And if you think Marauders are too confused or mad to know what Nephandi are, I reeeeeeeaaaaally suggest grabbing a copy of the Book Of Madness, First(!) Edition. It has a couple of facts and background on Marauders that were kept hush-hush in later writeups. Let's just say they are indeed a faction in the Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you decide that First edition Mage trumps the later editions, and most of the writers seem to claim the opposite.<br /> <br /> I've already said what I thought about how diverse marauders can be earlier in the post. But I stand by that interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T12:34:22-08:00","id":1020972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1020921#post1020921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if you decide that First edition Mage trumps the later editions, and most of the writers seem to claim the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The First Edition writeup doesn't contradict the later Editions at all (or vice versa). The opposite, First Ed completes it with behind-the-obvious-scenes information.<br /> Also, the M20 Anthology story about the Hermetic becoming a Marauder, interestingly enough, perfectly fits a crucial part of the First Ed lore <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> None of this, by the way, means that Marauders aren't very..very very and utterly individual. Quite the opposite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T16:27:55-08:00","id":1021430,"title":"","content":"Other than innate countermagic, are Nephandi affected by True Faith? Can they be near Holy Relics? Does being on Holy Ground cause them discomfort? Do Widderslainte use Qlippothic Spheres, or regular, non-corrupted ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T16:30:02-08:00","id":1021431,"title":"","content":"How do you redeem a Nephandus, other than turning it into a Marauder?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T16:31:57-08:00","id":1021432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1021430#post1021430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other than innate countermagic, are Nephandi affected by True Faith? Can they be near Holy Relics? Does being on Holy Ground cause them discomfort? Do Widderslainte use Qlippothic Spheres, or regular, non-corrupted ones?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On the whole, Nephandi don't have any one specific thing that they'd be affected by via Truth Faith. However, individual Nephandi can have all sorts of weaknesses just like any other mage. They might even pretend to have weaknesses in order to make the enemy think they've got the upper hand.<br /> <br /> Widderslainte have an inverted avatar, so they use the Qlippothic spheres. That being said, all nephandi are capable of doing the same kind of magic as any other mage. It just leaves a nasty resonance behind unless they've put effort into hiding it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T16:34:39-08:00","id":1021433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1021431#post1021431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you redeem a Nephandus, other than turning it into a Marauder?</div> </div> </div> </div>Canonically? You don't.<br /> <br /> The inversion of the avatar is a one way ticket. There are hints in the text that a nephandi needs to truly regret what they've done and then sacrifice themselves in order to restore their avatar, but that's never been confirmed.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think turning a Nephandi into a Marauder is a good choice. Give a nephandi the ability to avoid paradox and reshape the universe in their view, and that's just asking for unbridled destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T17:29:07-08:00","id":1021442,"title":"","content":"How obvious are Qlippothic Spheres? Do you need Prime and Dimensional Science to obscure their Resonance? They hide their Resonance behind the Marauder. My understanding is that Nephandi that turn Marauder cease being Nephandi. They become Marauders instead. Not that that would be safe or anything... ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T18:54:52-08:00","id":1021454,"title":"","content":"The beginning fiction of some of the Mage books leads me to believe it <i>can</i> be done, but probably only if you're a centuries old archmage who kills the Nephandus and tampers with the avatar's reincarnation cycle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T18:58:07-08:00","id":1021455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1021442#post1021442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How obvious are Qlippothic Spheres? Do you need Prime and Dimensional Science to obscure their Resonance? They hide their Resonance behind the Marauder. My understanding is that Nephandi that turn Marauder cease being Nephandi. They become Marauders instead. Not that that would be safe or anything... ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no hard mechanics on this. You can make their magic as obvious or a subtle as best benefits your story. It could be argued that part of the benefit of having an inverted avatar is that you are now much more difficult to read. When a mage tries to read your aura they may be unable to detect anything particularly untoward.<br /> Regarding their resonance, it's the same rules as anything else. Coincidental magic won't leave much of a trace, but Vulgar magic probably will, and the more vulgar it is, the greater the mark.<br /> Controlling resonance in and of itself can be a Mind effect, though Entropy 5 alone can arguably be used to assist in these kinds of things.<br /> Though for the most part a Nephandi can probably get away with their resonance simply because most mages can have completely legitimate reasons for having weird resonance. A necromancer is expected to have a little bit of Jhor on them, for example.<br /> <br /> From what I can tell, the main difference between the Qlippothic Spheres and the regular ones are that the Qlippothics just have an Entropic bend to them. Qlippothic Mind is all about exploiting the wholes in one's memory, the neurotic behaviours that lead to uncertainty and a lack of trust in ones own actions. Qlippothic Time is about eroding away at the time stream in order to distort and break down the natural flow of time. And Qlippothic Prime is about the draining of Quintessence, and the void that's left behind.<br /> <br /> The vast majority of this stuff will be similar to the kinds of things that Tradition Mages are capable off. It's only when they notice the Entropic tone of it all, or encounter something that only the Qlippothic spheres are capable of (such as draining quintessence from an unwilling Mage's own avatar) that the observant mage may realise something's not right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T20:38:35-08:00","id":1021464,"title":"","content":"They're New World Order. And there isn't much to go on about Technephandi in Mage 20. Of course. *sigh* Thanks for the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T05:01:57-08:00","id":1021531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1021464#post1021464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're New World Order. And there isn't much to go on about Technephandi in Mage 20. Of course. *sigh* Thanks for the help.</div> </div> </div> </div>They'll be like any other nephandi, except they'll be corrupting the Technocratic paradigm. Perhaps they make liberal use of Psychological techniques to gaslight their targets, of redefine and overuse words in order to destroy their meaning.<br /> Perhaps they take the Data sphere and use it to corrupt the distinction between information on either end, making a virus which can corrupt data from across the world just by casual association.<br /> <br /> It depends on the motives of the nephandus what effects they would go for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T14:26:10-08:00","id":1022093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>visigoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1019708#post1019708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These attempts only happen because nephandi are cohesive, organized, have an hierarchy and are apparently rational actors in the ascension war. Thus I as a player am baffled by the lack of rational justifications or reasons for their objectives. What they see in the cauls that lead them to act like they act? What they learnt from oblivion demons that they ended like this?<br /> School shooters, serial killers, rapists are lonely people with mental illness, not an organization with an agenda. Mafia, criminal organizations, militant groups are &quot;evil&quot; or &quot;wrong&quot; as long as they are marginalized, excluded or working illegally. Nephandi are none of these things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer the explanation that the Nephandi - even if they won't admit it - don't actually want the destruction of the world/reality. Descension isn't pure drive towards annihilation - instead, it is the thesis that it is in suffering, pain, terror and hopelessness that Reality's true potential and malleability are realized. And thus the most powerful True Magick can be worked within the Nephandic Paradigms. A Mage can become truly supreme over Reality only once weakness is expunged \u2013 and sadism, exploitation and ruthlessness are the natural pathways to doing so. The Nephandi used to be called Nif'ur en'Daah \u2013 Eaters of the Weak.<br /> Whether a given Nephandus follows Descension out of truly being a selfish and sadistic person, or follows it to gain greater power, probably varies from Nephandus to Nephandus. In the latter case it could be argued that it might be less of a inner philosophy, and more of an attitude towards Sleepers and larger Reality - exploitative rather than complementary; that shapes a Nephandus' Paradigm and style.<br /> <br /> Al-Aswad agreed to the Pact with the dark beings outside reality in return for power and being their majordomo. And...<br /> (Spoiler from the Hell on Earth scenario from the <i>Ascension</i> book)<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> ...In the end the world isn't destroyed. The beings from outside materialize on Earth and the Consensus shifts towards Descension; but the planet (and rest of Reality, I suppose) survives and is divided between various Nephandi, and Voormas :-P. The writing entertains the possibility of taking back the fight to the Nephandi. Slaves are described as building monuments to Al-Aswad. Seems like a cop out from the &quot;destroy reality&quot; pitch.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In W20 <i>Book of the Wyrm</i> a new camp of Black Spiral Dancers - the Princes of Ruin - is described as believing that the Apocalypse has already happened, and the Wyrm's chosen place is to rule over what's left and enjoy themselves. Thus, it might be that not all of the Malfean Nephandi want to destroy the world; the Wyrm has shifted from destruction to corruption, after all.<br /> Infernal Nephandi I can see wanting to recreate the Devil-King Age. Plus, it makes no sense that they would want to unmake the whole of Reality - after all, they are supposed to have sold their souls to the various Demon Lords, who want to rule over reality, as far as I'm aware of.<br /> The K'llasshaa likewise don't have to go for annihilation - there are plenty of beings in Lovecraft Mythos who are capable of more than mindless destruction. In Chamber's <i>The King in Yellow</i> two characters are pretty insane in the vein of the K'llasshaa \u2013 yet they still possess a rational goal of ruling the world.<br /> <br /> Jodi Blake, while successfully tempting a Chorister, says: \u201c<i>I used to think that pleasure was wrong as well, that all my 'sins' would ensure my immediate death and eternal suffering. It's been hundreds of years and, as you can see, I am quite happy and hardly suffering.</i>\u201d Now, she might not be sincere \u2013 but I'd like to think that Nephandi would be still able to experience the usual pleasures; or find satisfaction in amassing temporal and mystical power.<br /> <br /> Thus, the Cauls could be said to be more of an instrument in allowing a Mage to truly connect with a sadistic and selfish Paradigm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1021433#post1021433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inversion of the avatar is a one way ticket. There are hints in the text that a nephandi needs to truly regret what they've done and then sacrifice themselves in order to restore their avatar, but that's never been confirmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a Batini leader \u2013 Miriam Ben-Hamida - whose husband became Barrabi and tried to go on with his family life. She killed him and is described as starting a ritual to redeem his Avatar. Though this might be possibly because not much time passed since he became a Nephandus. It doesn't say whether the ritual was successful, but it mentions that it took two days to perform, and that due to the ritual she became a Master of the Spirit Sphere.<br /> Neville Sinclair Nevermore, the leader of the Hollow Ones, is rumoured to be a former Nephandus.<br /> <br /> I'd say the reasons why Nephandi are supposedly unredeemable are more complex than &quot;It can't be done.&quot; It can be done, but it is both extremely difficult and extremely dangerous. Not only you have to be wary of the one you want to help and other Nephandi; you also risk being killed or Gilgul'ed by other Mages. Finally, I like to think that a major reason why Nephandi can't be redeemed is that \u2013 especially once the previous two factors are taken into account \u2013 nobody cares enough to try. Why would someone risk their resources, time, effort, life, and possibly their very soul...for someone who made the choice to become a Nephandus in the first place? :&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-25-2016, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T20:38:09-08:00","id":1022199,"title":"","content":"I think the redemption of Marauders would be more interesting than the redemption of Nephandi. How would you reduce the Quiet of a Marauder? Even if you could not eliminate it, I imagine that reducing a Marauder from Quiet 5 to Quiet 1 would be considered to be quite an accomplishment (if you can convince a Marauder that she is not Goddess Isis, who cares if she believes that America uses metric units?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T14:09:10-08:00","id":1022449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1021433#post1021433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inversion of the avatar is a one way ticket. There are hints in the text that a nephandi needs to truly regret what they've done and then sacrifice themselves in order to restore their avatar, but that's never been confirmed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it's the &quot;The Nephandi must sacrifice themselves for redemption&quot; mentality that is problematic. Maybe there have been redeemed Nephandi, but all of them were convinced - or outright manipulated or Gaes'ed - to undertake forlorn hope etc. missions. I'd say that it makes more sense that to Un-invert an Avatar you must do more than sacrificing yourself - there are certainly many, many other ways to do good things in the world, that could lead the Mage and the Avatar away from Descension.<br /> Mages don't look for additional rituals and means to help the Nephandi because of this belief that they can only be redeemed through sacrifice.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1022199#post1022199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the redemption of Marauders would be more interesting than the redemption of Nephandi. How would you reduce the Quiet of a Marauder? Even if you could not eliminate it, I imagine that reducing a Marauder from Quiet 5 to Quiet 1 would be considered to be quite an accomplishment (if you can convince a Marauder that she is not Goddess Isis, who cares if she believes that America uses metric units?).</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>Book of Madness</i> suggests a possibility: &quot;<i>When entering a Quiet warp, players make a contested Arete roll against the Marauder. On a successful roll, reality reasserts itself via the mage. Normal reality radiates from her with a power equal to her Static Resonance trait. If her Static trait is greater or equal to the Marauder's Dynamic Resonance, the warp is nullified. The Marauder, of course, has no idea and behaves as a low-Resonance Marauder until the Mage leaves the area.</i>&quot; Thus an Arete 7 Ivory Tower Professor with a high Static (Rational) Resonance could prevent the Marauder-bubble warping.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is beating a Marauder at their own delusion \u2013 so a caveman Marauder might be wrestled down by one of Bluecho's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/661521-new-practice-primal-arts\">Primal Mages</a>. A Marauder living in video game might respect Virtual Adepts who convince him they are more pro. Combined with some custom rotes/effects, this might allow to subdue or reduce both Marauder's Quiet and their Marauder-bubble.<br /> <br /> A problem I see with helping Marauders is that you have to work with both the Avatar and the Mage. Technocracy would be well equipped to cure the issues in the psyche, reducing or subduing the Quiet. Mystic Mages would work better with the Avatar.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T16:14:13-08:00","id":1022507,"title":"","content":"We have an ordinary human who has True Faith 5. Six with the Spear. Nine with the Spear and Holy Ground. ^^ Erebus would just kill the wIdderslainte. The Cup of Dreams from Changeling might help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T17:00:19-08:00","id":1024002,"title":"","content":"If the widderslainte wants to resist, how do you do so, other than high willpower? Mind magic? Processing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T17:47:21-08:00","id":1024025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1004711-storytelling-nephandi-and-marauders?p=1024002#post1024002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the widderslainte wants to resist, how do you do so, other than high willpower? Mind magic? Processing it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on how powerful their tainted avatar is, and what can do to persuade the Widderslainte to succumb to their will.<br /> <br /> Who's to say high willpower, mind magic, drugs, or what not won't work on some? If it makes a good story, then go for it.<br /> <br /> Perhaps though, such techniques don't actually work, but their tainted avatar only lets them think it works, so that the mage lowers their guard and becomes comfortable, that's when the real persuasion begins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachm